  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/references/calendar.md"
    end_line: 85
    content: "# Google Calendar API\n\n## Scopes\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar` \342\200\224 See, edit, share, and\n    permanently delete all the calendars you can access using Google Calendar.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.acls` \342\200\224 See and change the sharing\n    permissions of Google calendars you own.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.acls.readonly` \342\200\224 See the sharing\n    permissions of Google calendars you own.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.app.created` \342\200\224 Make secondary\n    Google calendars, and see, create, change, and delete events on them.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendarlist` \342\200\224 See, add, and\n    remove Google calendars you\342\200\231re subscribed to.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendarlist.readonly` \342\200\224 See the\n    list of Google calendars you\342\200\231re subscribed to.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendars` \342\200\224 See and change the\n    properties of Google calendars you have access to, and create secondary\n    calendars.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendars.readonly` \342\200\224 See the\n    title, description, default time zone, and other properties of Google\n    calendars you have access to.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events` \342\200\224 View and edit events on\n    all your calendars.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.freebusy` \342\200\224 See the\n    availability on Google calendars you have access to.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.owned` \342\200\224 See, create,\n    change, and delete events on Google calendars you own.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.owned.readonly` \342\200\224 See the\n    events on Google calendars you own.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.public.readonly` \342\200\224 See the\n    events on public calendars.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.readonly` \342\200\224 View events on\n    all your calendars.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.freebusy` \342\200\224 View your availability\n    in your calendars.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly` \342\200\224 See and download any\n    calendar you can access using your Google Calendar.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.settings.readonly` \342\200\224 View your\n    Calendar settings.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n-   **Calendars**: Collections of events (primary or secondary).\n-   **Events**: Individual appointments with title, time, and location.\n-   **Attendees**: People invited to an event.\n-   **Reminders**: Notification settings for events.\n\n## Client-Side Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Example: List events\nconst res = await fetch(\'https://www.googleapis.com/calendar/v3/calendars/primary/events\', {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\n```\n\n## Server-Side Pattern (Next.js API Route)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/calendar/route.ts\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  const res = await fetch(\'https://www.googleapis.com/calendar/v3/calendars/primary/events\', {\n    headers: { Authorization: token! },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n"
    num_lines: 86
    num_bytes: 3140
    line_range_bytes: 3140
  }
}
