    content: "# Google Docs API\n\n## Scopes\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/documents` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete\n    all your Google Docs documents.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/documents.readonly` \342\200\224 See all your Google\n    Docs documents.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete all\n    of your Google Drive files.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file` \342\200\224 See, edit, create, and delete\n    only the specific Google Drive files you use with this app.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly` \342\200\224 See and download all your\n    Google Drive files.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n-   **Documents**: The top-level resource containing the document content.\n-   **BatchUpdate**: Method to send multiple write requests in a single call.\n-   **StructuralElements**: Components like Paragraphs, Tables, and Lists.\n-   **Paragraphs**: Text elements that can contain inline formatting.\n\n## Client-Side Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Example: Get document content\nconst res = await fetch(`https://docs.googleapis.com/v1/documents/${documentId}`, {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\n```\n\n## Server-Side Pattern (Next.js API Route)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/docs/route.ts\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  const { searchParams } = new URL(req.url);\n  const documentId = searchParams.get(\'documentId\');\n  const res = await fetch(`https://docs.googleapis.com/v1/documents/${documentId}`, {\n    headers: { Authorization: token! },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n"
    num_lines: 50
    num_bytes: 1618
    line_range_bytes: 1618
  }
}
