    content: "# Google Tasks API\n\n## Scopes\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks` \342\200\224 Create, edit, organize, and delete\n    all your tasks.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks.readonly` \342\200\224 View your tasks.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n-   **TaskLists**: Containers for tasks (e.g., \"Personal\", \"Work\").\n-   **Tasks**: Individual to-do items.\n-   **Due dates**: Deadlines associated with tasks.\n-   **Status**: Whether a task is completed or needs action.\n\n## Client-Side Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// List task lists\nconst res = await fetch(\'https://tasks.googleapis.com/tasks/v1/users/@me/lists\', {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\nconst data = await res.json();\n```\n\n## Server-Side Pattern (Next.js API Route)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/tasks/route.ts\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  const res = await fetch(\'https://tasks.googleapis.com/tasks/v1/users/@me/lists\', {\n    headers: { Authorization: token! },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n"
