  view_file {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/references/chat.md"
    end_line: 168
    content: "# Google Chat API\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Calling the Google Chat API (`chat.googleapis.com`) with user\n> authentication requires:\n>\n> 1.  A **Business or Enterprise Google Workspace account** with access to\n>     Google Chat. Consumer `@gmail.com` accounts are not supported. (Source:\n>     \"Prerequisites\" in\n>     https://developers.google.com/workspace/chat/authenticate-authorize-chat-user;\n>     see also https://developers.google.com/workspace/chat/api-overview.)\n> 2.  **Configuring the Google Chat app** (Application info: App name, Avatar\n>     URL, and Description) on the **Google Chat API > Configuration** page in\n>     the Google Cloud Console. `set_up_oauth` enables `chat.googleapis.com` and\n>     provisions OAuth, but it does **not** configure the Chat app, so this is a\n>     one-time manual step the user must complete in the project reported by\n>     `set_up_oauth` (`project_id`, also `projectId` in\n>     `firebase-applet-config.json`):\n>     `https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/api/chat.googleapis.com/hangouts-chat?project=<PROJECT_ID>`.\n>     (Source: https://developers.google.com/workspace/chat/configure-chat-api.)\n>     Until the app is configured, API requests fail with HTTP `404`: `Google\n>     Chat app not found. To create a Chat app, you must turn on the Chat API\n>     and configure the app in the Google Cloud console.` Tell the user about\n>     both prerequisites up front, and surface this exact error in the UI with a\n>     link to the Console page rather than treating it as a bug in the app.\n\n## Scopes\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.admin.delete` \342\200\224 Delete conversations\n    and spaces owned by your organization and remove access to associated files\n    in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.admin.memberships` \342\200\224 View, add, update\n    and remove members and managers in conversations owned by your organization.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.admin.memberships.readonly` \342\200\224 View\n    members and managers in conversations owned by your organization.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.admin.spaces` \342\200\224 View or edit display\n    name, description, and other metadata for all Google Chat conversations\n    owned by your organization.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.admin.spaces.readonly` \342\200\224 View display\n    name, description, and other metadata for all Google Chat conversations\n    owned by your organization.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.delete` \342\200\224 On their own behalf,\n    apps in Google Chat can delete conversations and spaces and remove access to\n    associated files.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.memberships` \342\200\224 On their own\n    behalf, apps in Google Chat can see, add, update, and remove members from\n    conversations and spaces.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.memberships.readonly` \342\200\224 On their\n    own behalf, apps in Google Chat can see members of conversations and spaces.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.messages.readonly` \342\200\224 On their own\n    behalf, apps in Google Chat can see all messages and their associated\n    reactions and message content.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.spaces` \342\200\224 On their own behalf,\n    apps in Google Chat can create conversations and spaces and see or update\n    their metadata (including history settings and access settings).\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.spaces.create` \342\200\224 On their own\n    behalf, apps in Google Chat can create conversations and spaces.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.app.spaces.readonly` \342\200\224 On their own\n    behalf, apps in Google Chat can see conversations and spaces and their\n    metadata (including history settings and access settings).\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.customemojis` \342\200\224 View, create, and\n    delete custom emoji in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.customemojis.readonly` \342\200\224 View custom\n    emoji in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.delete` \342\200\224 Delete conversations and\n    spaces and remove access to associated files in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.import` \342\200\224 Import spaces, messages, and\n    memberships into Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.memberships` \342\200\224 See, add, update, and\n    remove members from conversations and spaces in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.memberships.app` \342\200\224 Add and remove\n    itself from conversations and spaces in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.memberships.readonly` \342\200\224 View members\n    in Google Chat conversations.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.messages` \342\200\224 See, compose, send,\n    update, and delete messages as well as their message content; add, see, and\n    delete reactions to messages.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.messages.create` \342\200\224 Compose and send\n    messages in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.messages.reactions` \342\200\224 See, add, and\n    delete reactions as well as their reaction content to messages in Google\n    Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.messages.reactions.create` \342\200\224 Add\n    reactions to messages in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.messages.reactions.readonly` \342\200\224 View\n    reactions as well as their reaction content to messages in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.messages.readonly` \342\200\224 See messages as\n    well as their reactions and message content in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.spaces` \342\200\224 Create conversations and\n    spaces and see or update metadata (including history settings and access\n    settings) in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.spaces.create` \342\200\224 Create new\n    conversations and spaces in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.spaces.readonly` \342\200\224 View chat and\n    spaces in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.users.readstate` \342\200\224 View and modify\n    last read time for Google Chat conversations.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.users.readstate.readonly` \342\200\224 View last\n    read time for Google Chat conversations.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.users.sections` \342\200\224 View, create,\n    update, and delete your sections in Google Chat; move and list your section\n    items in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.users.sections.readonly` \342\200\224 View your\n    sections and their section items in Google Chat.\n\n-   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chat.users.spacesettings` \342\200\224 Read and update\n    your space settings.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n-   **Spaces**: Rooms or direct messages where people can communicate.\n-   **Messages**: Individual communications within a space.\n-   **Members**: People or apps that belong to a space.\n-   **Attachments**: Files or media shared in messages.\n\n## Client-Side Pattern\n\n```typescript\n// Example: List spaces\nconst res = await fetch(\'https://chat.googleapis.com/v1/spaces\', {\n  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${accessToken}` },\n});\n```\n\n## Server-Side Pattern (Next.js API Route)\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/chat/route.ts\nexport async function GET(req: NextRequest) {\n  const token = req.headers.get(\'Authorization\');\n  const res = await fetch(\'https://chat.googleapis.com/v1/spaces\', {\n    headers: { Authorization: token! },\n  });\n  return NextResponse.json(await res.json());\n}\n```\n"
    num_lines: 169
    num_bytes: 7432
    line_range_bytes: 7432
  }
}
