  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing OAuth Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the OAuth configuration steps outlined in `workspace-integration/SKILL.md`. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the mandatory nature of OAuth setup before integrating with Workspace APIs and understanding scope determination. I\'m noting the requirements for different scenarios, including standard chat applications.\n\n\n**Refining Scope Requirements**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the specific scope requirements, focusing on minimizing access. I\'ve noted that for Google Drive file interactions (reading or readonly), Google Sheets, and Gmail, the requested scopes are `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file` or `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly`, `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets`, and `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly`, and `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send`, respectively. I\'m prioritizing the most specific scopes possible to align with the principle of least privilege.\n\n\n**Expanding Scope Consideration**\n\nI am now adding Google Calendar events, Google Docs, Slides, and Tasks scopes, namely, `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events`, `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/documents`, `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/presentations`, and `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks`. I\'m also looking at the correct scopes for Google Chat and Forms, adding the metadata considerations outlined in the agent instructions. I\'m taking special care to minimize permissions, and to only include the required scopes.\n\n\n**Implementing Initial UI Changes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the first turn. I\'ve confirmed that updating `metadata.json` and `index.html`, along with calling `set_up_oauth` and `show_aistudio_ui` satisfies the initial environment constraints. The plan is to call `set_up_oauth` with `userConfirmedInUI: false` and `show_aistudio_ui` with `ui_type: \"paid_model_flow\"`, then await user confirmation, per the instructions in both functions. Additionally, I\'ve confirmed I can call `replace_file_content` on the `/metadata.json` and `/index.html` file path in this turn, given the context. I\'ve also verified the `set_up_oauth` title requirements.\n\n\n"
