  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Rejecting Google Integration**\n\nI\'ve decided to decline the Google Workspace OAuth flow. No Google Drive, Sheets, Gmail, Calendar, Docs, Slides, or Tasks for me. I\'m rejecting the integration entirely.\n\n\n**Building E-Commerce Platform**\n\nI\'m now fully committed to building the \"Pretty Charm\" e-commerce platform from scratch. I\'ve formulated a detailed verification plan focused on customer journeys, especially the guest checkout flow. This includes browsing the storefront, verifying product states (draft vs. active), adding active items to the cart, and completing a guest order with a valid Indian delivery address.\n\n\n**Verifying Order Flow**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the order verification process. I\'m focusing on \"Track My Order\" functionality, ensuring phone number validation, proper order status display, and honest delivery estimates. I\'m also confirming that it rejects incorrect phone numbers. I\'ve built a testing plan to confirm this is working as expected.\n\n\n**Defining Platform Scope**\n\nI\'ve outlined the complete feature set, including all 23 customer-facing screens, interactive 3D elements like a gift box viewer using Three.js, and AI-powered features. Additionally, I\'ve specified a comprehensive 15-section admin panel. Furthermore, the visual style includes a blush pink, warm cream, and rose-gold palette with refined serif headings paired with clean sans body font.\n\n\n**Listing Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now identifying and gathering all the necessary dependencies. I\'m focusing on the frontend, listing packages such as `three` and its types for the 3D viewer, `xlsx` for spreadsheet exports, `vite-plugin-pwa` for PWA capabilities, and `better-sqlite3` along with its types for a robust SQLite database. I\'m aiming for a comprehensive inventory of visual slots upfront.\n\n\n"
