  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a solid start. The required dependencies, including three.js, relevant types, and plugins for Excel and Progressive Web App functionality, are installed without issue. Now, the real work begins: I\'m diving into full-stack architecture and modular file structure design to address all the project\'s requirements systematically. This will take time!\n\n\n**Defining Core Logic**\n\nI\'ve completed the architectural blueprint for the core domain logic, it\'s all implemented in `/src/shared/domainLogic.ts`. Key features are now fully functional, including currency arithmetic with paise calculations, the shipping rules engine with Indian PIN code validation and configurable tiers, and catalogue publication rules to manage product statuses and purchasing permissions. The logic is cleanly separated, testable, and addresses all project constraints.\n\n\n**Calculating Inventory Metrics**\n\nI\'m working on the inventory management system. I\'m focusing on handling out-of-stock scenarios. The WAC calculation is now functional, including preserving historical cost data for accurate profit reporting. Also, I\'m designing state machines for order, payment, cancellation, and refund processes. I\'m tracking order status (Pending, Confirmed, etc.), payment status (Pending, Paid, Refunded, etc.), and shipment status (Not Shipped, In Transit, etc.).\n\n\n**Implementing Delivery Workflow**\n\nI\'m now implementing the delivery workflow, including tracking order status with states such as \'Out for Delivery\', \'Delivered\', and \'RTO\'. I\'m also ensuring stock reservation during valid order creation and atomic release upon cancellation. I\'ve added duplicate order detection and phone number normalization for \'Track My Order\'. Additionally, I\'ve incorporated deduplication for courier webhook events, a reliable ETA display, and a secure WhatsApp Click-to-Chat URL builder.\n\n\n**Refining Order Processes**\n\nI\'m focused on the edge cases within the order processes. Right now, I\'m working on several refinements. I\'ve got configurable shipping calculations based on order value, server-side price recalculation, and guest checkout with Indian PIN and mobile validation. I\'ve also implemented duplicate order submission prevention. Plus, I\'ve integrated robust payment verification and inventory concurrency management to prevent overselling. Further, I\'m improving cancellation and stock release procedures, and also order lookups with phone number verification. Finally, I\'m preventing invalid lookups and webhook deduplication.\n\n\n**Constructing the Database**\n\nI\'ve just finished setting up the persistent relational SQLite database using `node:sqlite`. It\'s housed in `/src/server/db.ts` and uses a JSON backup. All 18 relational tables are created with proper foreign keys, indexes, and ACID transactions. I\'ve also seeded the required categories, including ones marked \'coming-soon\' for Cosmetics & Beauty.\n\n\n**Seeding the Database**\n\nI\'m now populating the database. I\'m seeding a \"Festive Collection\" category with a \"coming-soon\" status and badge, adding four draft hampers to it. Each hamper has a proposed price and draft status. Furthermore, I\'m seeding real Hair Accessories & Jewellery products, complete with variants, SKUs, costs, stock levels, and bespoke artwork to make the storefront shoppable even with unpublished items. There is a safe admin bootstrap mechanism implemented via environment variables for secure initial setup.\n\n\n**Securing Backend Access**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust security measures in `/server.ts`. I\'ve added salted password hashing (PBKDF2-SHA512), HTTP-only session cookies, a bearer session token, and rate limiting to protect the APIs. Full audit logging is also in place for all interactions.\n\n\n\n**Integrating AI Models**\n\nI\'m now integrating the AI models. I\'ve successfully connected to the Google GenAI models and made `/gift-finder`, `/api/ai/image-generate`, `/api/ai/image-edit`, `/api/ai/video-generate`, `/api/ai/search-trends`, and `/api/ai/maps-grounding` endpoints, using various Gemini models (3.8-flash, 4-argon, etc.) through `ai.interactions.create`.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nMy focus has shifted to the frontend and AI integrations. I\'ve designed modular components in `/src/components/`, starting with `/src/assets/productArtwork.ts` which has all the high-resolution luxury SVG data-URI illustrations. I\'m also building an interactive 3D Gift Hamper & Jewellery Box Studio with Three.js in `/src/components/ThreeHamperViewer.tsx`.\n\n\n**Constructing Interactive Studio**\n\nI\'m now deep in frontend development. I\'m focusing on crafting a visually rich and interactive user experience. I\'m building a 3D Gift Hamper & Jewellery Box Studio with Three.js. It features a claw, rose-gold earrings, and a velvet cushion. I\'m also using warm/cool 3-point lighting, a radial contact shadow, and implementing on-demand `requestRender()` and `afterDraw()` rendering, along with a collapsible bottom control dock.\n\n\n"
