  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining API Exports**\n\nI\'ve got a much clearer picture now. I\'ve pinpointed the exact API contract thanks to `server.ts` and am now reviewing the precise exports from those various components: `domainLogic.ts`, `productArtwork.ts`, and the React components: `ThreeHamperViewer.tsx`, `GeminiStudioModal.tsx`, and `Admin.tsx`. This helps clarify the data flow and how everything interacts.\n\n\n**Pinpointing API Consumers**\n\nI am now focusing on the consumer side, specifically how `Dashboard.tsx` utilizes various exports. From the shared domain logic, I see functions like `formatINR` and `calculateCustomerShippingFeePaise` are critical. I also observe the usage of `ARTWORK` and specific React components, including `ThreeHamperViewer`, `GeminiStudioModal`, and `AdminDashboard`, complete with their prop requirements. Additionally, I am enumerating the public API routes and their request/response schemas.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_321223"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add data/*.sqlite and playwright-report to .gitignore\", \"EndLine\":9, \"Instruction\":\"Append SQLite data directory and test artifacts to .gitignore\", \"ReplacementContent\":\".env*\\n!.env.example\\ndata/*.sqlite\\ndata/*.sqlite-*\\nplaywright-report/\\ntest-results/\\n\", \"StartLine\":7, \"TargetContent\":\".env*\\n!.env.example\\n\", \"TargetFile\":\"/.gitignore\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating .gitignore\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update .gitignore\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\205\023\n\202\023\001i\024}\023\024\020u\315\362s0\245\022\214Z\210O\305v-\225\\\b\b\221\252y\203\244a/\377m\255!\345:\316\235&\020\273]r3\244d\255\340\200\234\367\336W\032$Z\016\020\243\b=\000\267\f@\323Ybn|\201\363\2132\250\032\367\301J\272\356N\017\222\3065g\300e&:PEL\023e\206\242f+\200zia\f\215\376|\"N\260#\362\346\037\206\032\376\306\234\304\016w\267*Z\\\v\366\357_\301\374\020Kwn\314\201\372\002\363B\033\031\027\366\334\214*S\364\177\332\021Cn\317 e\270\231&\345Uh\363\031\n\n\036\377\022\200&\f\301\376\231\026\307$UY\371\324\265\'\f(1\036\374\367\202\tK\200z\326\256<\262Zu\227\306n\266\202\024i\3035\243\036\321F\367\210\025\377/\337sw\253\023^\032\n\004\250}BG2\367\372\353I7Md\320\n\255H\016\317\336\350*8\323\257\240\\\313\233\223\313\034\356y:\377\206\365\246)\253jr\214\205\321\202p\375\203\341\336}5\3620\037\373\326\312@\320!\222\256\340\346\3047\375\321\376\206\232eW\332\363\214S\326\036\b\264\3118\360eo\367\237M1\347\244`\237\337\346\225\032\a\331\336\353\030((0\205\360\002\3660\bl)\337\227\310\034\301\251\305X\243\320\310\003\212;\254\204\312\300~&\221|#\027^\353.\232\241\324\344b:\235:\210\215p\346\355VE\215:#\376\373\316\253{\307m\340\017\001U\227\263\350\255\2407\310\221\016\213\271\215N<F\377gXW\207\263\270\232d\263oa}\202Gh\336\264J\314\230\257\215Q\377\202~\206\354\0341\272\206Km\221RP? ^\356\203\256\2276\211X\226\266\203\270d\270\005\374+\035\240^^\202\n\215\223\343\032\345M\355q\235\227$&7\277\226v\230\aE\225\000\312\340\017\234\347-\236\342\333?cO\352*E\3079\234\350\272\210\363Q\360N\225\311 \340\211\206YkJ/R}\002\3358\352\210\250\241\2404\355V\026i\215\305\031\320yi0\016!G\347t\265\374V\225\005.\201\325uB=3\240\235\277\357-\r^*\362\026\272\024\\\300<0i&\233\n,s\211\034rD\373[\207bt\035:m\v\371&d\240\3308g\217\335\037\2344\005\335m\263\262\016\332\320l\221\362*\205\"vTE\222R\a\273\220\324\307-\255\a\005\232\206\001\322fC8\016Tn\372l\263!\031\276:KI\215\224~r_\360\236LfF\351w\t\327a\307\275\311^H\375\232\f\334-\210\2