  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Date Issues**\n\nI\'m now investigating a timestamp issue. Initially, I seeded the database using `db.ts`, but noticed that all the products got the same `created_at` value. It seems using `const now = new Date().toISOString();` in a single loop produced this result. Further, I see `createdAt` is stripped in the `publicProducts` function in `server.ts`.\n\n\n**Addressing Date Handling**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the omission of `createdAt` and `updatedAt` in `/api/storefront` responses. This explains the identical `created_at` values in the database and why sorting by `\"Newest Arrivals\"` was failing. The `publicProducts` function in `server.ts` was stripping these fields. Now I am digging into `domainLogic.ts` and how it handles both `categories` and `shop` screens.\n\n\n**Defining Sort Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently working on a pure function, `sortCatalogueProducts`, for sorting product catalogues. I\'ve defined `ProductSortOption` with options like \'featured\', \'price-asc\', \'price-desc\', and \'newest\'. The sorting logic for each option is now clearly defined. Next, I\'ll be adding unit tests in `domainLogic.test.ts` to verify the functionality of `sortCatalogueProducts` with different sort options.\n\n\n**Implementing Date Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring `createdAt` and `updatedAt` are correctly included in the `/api/storefront` responses by adding them to `publicProducts` in `server.ts`. I also need to stagger timestamps for seeded products in `db.ts` to ensure \"Newest Arrivals\" works. I\'ll make sure to create a migration for `initializeDatabase()` to handle any existing identical timestamps. Finally, I\'ll leverage `sortCatalogueProducts` in `App.tsx` for proper product sorting, ensuring no input mutation, and implement the product listing enhancements in the view.\n\n\n"
