  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating Database Seeding**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring the `created_at` timestamps for seeded products in `src/server/db.ts` are distinct and staggered. If I find existing databases with identical timestamps, I plan to implement an update to differentiate these values.\n\n\n**Implementing Sorting Options**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the sort functionality. I\'m importing `sortCatalogueProducts`, `PRODUCT_SORT_OPTIONS`, and `ProductSortOption` into `src/App.tsx`. I\'m updating `filteredProducts` to use the imported `sortCatalogueProducts` function, using the `sortBy` value. Both the shop and categories views will have a sort select dropdown and quick-select buttons with the specified labels. This includes the category cards\' sorted product listings, too.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_279271"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Ensure seeded products have distinct staggered created_at timestamps so Newest Arrivals sorting produces a deterministic chronological order\", \"EndLine\":674, \"Instruction\":\"Add idempotent staggered created_at timestamps for seeded catalogue items in src/server/db.ts\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"      for (const v of p.variants) {\\n        insertVariant.run(\\n          v.id,\\n          p.id,\\n          v.name,\\n          v.sku,\\n          v.delta,\\n          v.stock,\\n          0,\\n          now,\\n          now\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  // Ensure initial seeded catalogue items have distinct created_at timestamps for \'Newest Arrivals\' sorting\\n  const distinctTimestamps = db\\n    .prepare(\'SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT created_at) as c FROM products\')\\n    .get() as { c: number };\\n  if (distinctTimestamps.c <= 1) {\\n    const staggeredOrder = [\\n      \'prod-mini-hamper\',\\n      \'prod-bestie-box\',\\n      \'prod-premium-box\',\\n      \'prod-celebration-box\',\\n      \'prod-pearl-claw\',\\n      \'prod-satin-bow-barrette\',\\n      \'prod-silk-scrunchie-trio\',\\n      \'prod-pearl-drop-huggies\',\\n      \'prod-charm-bracelet\',\\n      \'prod-quartz-necklace\',\\n    ];\\n    const baseMs = Date.parse(\'2026-10-10T10:00:00.000Z\');\\n    const updateCreated = db.prepare(\'UPDATE products SET created_at = ? WHERE id = ?\');\\n    staggeredOrder.forEach((prodId, idx) => {\\n      const ts = new Date(baseMs + idx * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();\\n      updateCreated.run(ts, prodId);\\n    });\\n  }\\n\", \"StartLine\":657, \"TargetContent\":\"      for (const v of p.variants) {\\n        insertVariant.run(\\n          v.id,\\n          p.id,\\n          v.name,\\n          v.sku,\\n          v.delta,\\n          v.stock,\\n          0,\\n          now,\\n          now\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/server/db.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding staggered product timestamps in src/server/db.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add staggered product timestamps in db.ts\"}"
