  planner_response {
    response: "Product sorting has been implemented for the Product Listing and Category views:\n\n- **Sorting Options**: Added support for sorting products by **`Price: Low to High`**, **`Price: High to Low`**, **`Newest Arrivals`**, and **`Featured`**.\n- **Interactive Controls**: Users can switch sort order using either the **Sort dropdown** or the **quick-select sort buttons** on both the Product Listing (`Shop Collection`) and `Categories` views, with a live summary displaying the active sort mode and matching product count.\n- **Chronological & Price Accuracy**: Exposed product creation timestamps (`createdAt`) from the storefront API, ensured distinct timestamps across catalogue entries, and added unit-tested pure sorting logic (`sortCatalogueProducts`) verifying price ascending, price descending, and newest arrivals ordering."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Interface Design**\n\nI\'ve been examining the image `pc-shop-sorting.png`. The interface seems exceptionally clean and well-organized. I especially noticed the synchronized behavior between the `<select>` dropdown and the quick-select buttons. Also, the active sort summary displaying \"Showing 10 products\" looks very solid.\n\n\n"
