    thinking: "**Analyzing Product Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the initial product data from the database. I\'ve begun with the ten existing products, starting with `prod-bestie-box` and `prod-celebration-box`. My initial focus is on understanding the product names, categories, SKUs, and associated metadata. I am working to understand the structure of the data to begin making associations, comparisons and deriving insights.\n\n\n**Examining Product Details**\n\nNow, I\'m diving deeper into specific product attributes. I\'ve noted each product\'s status (`active` or `draft`), prices, SKUs, and, most importantly, any variants. I\'m paying close attention to the variants, such as color and size options, for the `hair-accessories` and `jewellery`. This should lead to potential insights on how we can structure the information better.\n\n\n**Locating Product Images**\n\nI\'m now moving on to the next task which is locating the original product images. I\'ve broken down the process into defined steps, starting with searching for matches using specific product information. My approach includes using the product name, brand, variant, and SKU, prioritizing official sources and authorized distributors. I will meticulously verify image accuracy and check for quality and permissions, rejecting any AI-generated or unverified images.\n\n\n**Defining Image Handling Rules**\n\nI\'m now formulating concrete rules for image handling. It includes a multi-step process for new images, starting with locating and verifying them. I\'ll need to define how to handle image updates after approval, preserving all other product data. Finally, I\'m working to outline an admin report to display product image statuses and ensure security and compliance in the image search process.\n\n\n"
