  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Details**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the prompt\'s specific directives, particularly the constraints outlined in Steps 2 through 5. My goal is to ensure I\'m adhering precisely to each requirement. I\'m carefully reviewing the instructions to avoid any substitutions and to maintain accuracy.\n\n\n**Clarifying Image Search Criteria**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the image acquisition workflow. I\'m prioritizing the steps for incorporating an authorized image, including admin approval and image gallery updating. Additionally, I am ensuring to accurately manage product data, especially preserving the original product ID, price, and description. I am also planning how to preserve existing images.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Compliance & Licensing**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the technical and safety rules, ensuring strict adherence. The emphasis is on avoiding any unauthorized image use, especially from third-party retailers. I\'m prioritizing the use of licensed sources, and the protection of the Pretty Charm UI and bespoke SKUs. I am very aware that no image may overwrite or replace any existing authorized image without express admin approval.\n\n\n**Implementing the Image Audit**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the technical implementation. I\'m focusing on integrating the entire product photo sourcing, verification, and approval workflow, complete with an admin image report, directly into the database, server, and Admin Panel. I\'m building out the `product_image_audit` record with precise fields, including status tracking. The primary goal is to maintain the database\'s integrity while providing a robust audit trail.\n\n\n**Refining Image Search APIs**\n\nI am now focusing on the server-side image search APIs, specifically the `/api/admin/product-images/search/:productId` endpoint and the bulk search. I\'m prioritizing the Wikimedia Commons API integration, ensuring I can execute precise queries. Additionally, I am designing the Gemini Search integration, conditional on an API key, to enhance search results. It is important to me that I establish a process to validate whether results from third-party markets match SKUs, with a focus on rejecting unverified images and protecting Pretty Charm\'s brand and SKUs. I am documenting the rejection of images.\n\n\n**Documenting Image Status**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the image status for specified products. I\'ve noted that draft hampers need photography, and hair/jewelry items require either confirmed sources or permission validation. For these active items, the audit findings are documented, including potential third-party URLs or CC-licensed candidates. I\'m prioritizing building the admin tools for authorized image uploads and searches against Wikimedia Commons.\n\n\n**Defining Approval Workflow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the image approval workflow via endpoints like `/api/admin/product-images/approve/:productId` with precise options: preserve, replace, or set as primary, updating `products.images_json` only after confirmation, ensuring product details stay untouched. I\'m also planning the rejection endpoint, `/api/admin/product-images/reject/:productId`, marking products appropriately. Plus, I am also considering a dual-access Admin Image Report, both in the dashboard and via an API endpoint. I will first design this in domain logic, and then move on to unit tests.\n\n\n**Defining Domain Logic Functions**\n\nI\'m now determining essential pure functions for `src/shared/domainLogic.ts`. I\'ll introduce `ProductImageAuditStatus` and `PRODUCT_IMAGE_AUDIT_STATUSES` to manage image audit statuses. Additionally, the `validateCandidateProductImage` function is being defined to assess image validity based on origin, format, and permission, with clear rejection reasons. I will focus on the validity checks and associated error messages.\n\n\n**Defining Image Integrity Checks**\n\nI\'m now formulating two new pure functions in `src/shared/domainLogic.ts`. First, `validateImageFormatAndSize` validates images based on format (e.g., `image/png`, `image/webp`) and size (<= 10MB), returning a status and reason. Second, `applyApprovedProductImageToGallery` manages image integration, never mutates existing images, and handles preserve/replace modes with the `setAsPrimary` option, deduplicating image arrays.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_306451"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Add ProductImageAuditStatus, validateCandidateProductImage, applyApprovedProductImageToGallery, and verifyCatalogueIntegrityUnchanged to src/shared/domainLogic.ts\", \"EndLine\":810, \"Instruction\":\"Add Section 11 for original product photo validation, approval gallery update, and catalogue integrity verification\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"    // Default \'featured\': active products first, then featured flag, then price ascending\\n    const aActive = a.status === \'active\' ? 1 : 0;\\n    const bActive = b.status === \'active\' ? 1 : 0;\\n    if (aActive !== bActive) return bActive - aActive;\\n\\n    const aFeatured = a.featured ? 1 : 0;\\n    const bFeatured = b.featured ? 1 : 0;\\n    if (aFeatured !== bFeatured) return bFeatured - aFeatured;\\n\\n    return a.sellingPricePaise - b.sellingPricePaise;\\n  });\\n  return copy;\\n}\\n\\n// ============================================================================\\n// 11. ORIGINAL PRODUCT PHOTO VERIFICATION, APPROVAL & INTEGRITY AUDIT\\n// ============================================================================\\n\\nexport type ProductImageAuditStatus =\\n  | \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\'\\n  | \'Image successfully added\'\\n  | \'Image Needed\'\\n  | \'Source or reuse permission unverified\'\\n  | \'Search failed\';\\n\\nexport const PRODUCT_IMAGE_AUDIT_STATUSES: ReadonlyArray<ProductImageAuditStatus> = [\\n  \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\',\\n  \'Image successfully added\',\\n  \'Image Needed\',\\n  \'Source or reuse permission unverified\',\\n  \'Search failed\',\\n];\\n\\nexport interface CandidateImageValidationInput {\\n  urlOrDataUri: string;\\n  sourceUrl: string;\\n  mimeType?: string;\\n  byteLength?: number;\\n  isAiGenerated?: boolean;\\n  hasReusePermission?: boolean;\\n  exactProductMatch?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateCandidateProductImage(\\n  input: CandidateImageValidationInput\\n): {\\n  valid: boolean;\\n  recommendedStatus: ProductImageAuditStatus;\\n  reason: string;\\n} {\\n  if (input.isAiGenerated) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Rejected: AI-generated images cannot be treated as genuine original product photographs.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.exactProductMatch === false) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Rejected: Candidate image does not match the exact product, packaging, colour, and variant.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.hasReusePermission === false) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Source or reuse permission unverified\',\\n      reason: \'Candidate image found on third-party domain, but commercial reuse permission or official brand authorization is unverified.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const rawUrl = String(input.urlOrDataUri || \'\').trim();\\n  const rawSource = String(input.sourceUrl || \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawUrl || !rawSource) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Both a valid image preview URL/file and an attribution source URL are required.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const isHttpsUrl = /^https:\\\\/\\\\/[^\\\\s]+$/i.test(rawUrl);\\n  const isRasterDataUri = /^data:image\\\\/(jpeg|jpg|png|webp);base64,[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+$/i.test(rawUrl);\\n  if (!isHttpsUrl && !isRasterDataUri) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Image must be a validated HTTPS photograph URL or a genuine JPEG/PNG/WebP photograph file.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.mimeType) {\\n    const allowedMimes = [\'image/jpeg\', \'image/jpg\', \'image/png\', \'image/webp\'];\\n    if (!allowedMimes.includes(input.mimeType.toLowerCase())) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        reason: `Unsupported image MIME type \\\"${input.mimeType}\\\". Only real JPEG, PNG, or WebP photographs are accepted.`,\\n      };\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  if (typeof input.byteLength === \'number\') {\\n    if (input.byteLength < 128) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        reason: \'Downloaded image file is empty or corrupted (< 128 bytes).\',\\n      };\\n    }\\n    if (input.byteLength > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        reason: \'Image file exceeds the 10 MB safety limit.\',\\n      };\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    valid: true,\\n    recommendedStatus: \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\',\\n    reason: \'Verified matching product photograph from permitted source \342\200\224 awaiting Admin approval before publishing.\',\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function applyApprovedProductImageToGallery(\\n  existingImages: readonly string[],\\n  approvedImageUrl: string,\\n  options: { replaceExisting: boolean; setAsPrimary: boolean }\\n): string[] {\\n  const cleanApproved = String(approvedImageUrl || \'\').trim();\\n  if (!cleanApproved) {\\n    return [...existingImages];\\n  }\\n\\n  if (options.replaceExisting) {\\n    return [cleanApproved];\\n  }\\n\\n  const filteredExisting = existingImages.filter((img) => img !== cleanApproved);\\n  if (options.setAsPrimary || filteredExisting.length === 0) {\\n    return [cleanApproved, ...filteredExisting];\\n  }\\n\\n  return [...filteredExisting, cleanApproved];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CatalogueIntegritySnapshot {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  slug: string;\\n  categorySlug: string;\\n  sku: string;\\n  sellingPricePaise: number;\\n  stockQty: number;\\n  status: string;\\n  variantSkus: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport function verifyCatalogueIntegrityUnchanged(\\n  before: ReadonlyArray<CatalogueIntegritySnapshot>,\\n  after: ReadonlyArray<CatalogueIntegritySnapshot>\\n): { unchanged: boolean; discrepancies: string[] } {\\n  const discrepancies: string[] = [];\\n\\n  if (before.length !== after.length) {\\n    discrepancies.push(`Product count changed from ${before.length} to ${after.length}.`);\\n  }\\n\\n  const beforeMap = new Map(before.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\\n  const afterMap = new Map(after.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\\n\\n  for (const [id, b] of beforeMap.entries()) {\\n    const a = afterMap.get(id);\\n    if (!a) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Existing product \\\"${b.name}\\\" (${id}) was removed.`);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    if (b.name !== a.name) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} name changed from \\\"${b.name}\\\" to \\\"${a.name}\\\".`);\\n    if (b.slug !== a.slug) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} slug changed.`);\\n    if (b.categorySlug !== a.categorySlug) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} category changed.`);\\n    if (b.sku !== a.sku) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} SKU changed from \\\"${b.sku}\\\" to \\\"${a.sku}\\\".`);\\n    if (b.sellingPricePaise !== a.sellingPricePaise) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} price changed from ${b.sellingPricePaise} to ${a.sellingPricePaise}.`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.stockQty !== a.stockQty) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} stock changed from ${b.stockQty} to ${a.stockQty}.`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.status !== a.status) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} status changed from \\\"${b.status}\\\" to \\\"${a.status}\\\".`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.variantSkus.join(\'|\') !== a.variantSkus.join(\'|\')) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} variants changed.`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const id of afterMap.keys()) {\\n    if (!beforeMap.has(id)) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Unexpected new product ID \\\"${id}\\\" was added.`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    unchanged: discrepancies.length === 0,\\n    discrepancies,\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"StartLine\":794, \"TargetContent\":\"    // Default \'featured\': active products first, then featured flag, then price ascending\\n    const aActive = a.status === \'active\' ? 1 : 0;\\n    const bActive = b.status === \'active\' ? 1 : 0;\\n    if (aActive !== bActive) return bActive - aActive;\\n\\n    const aFeatured = a.featured ? 1 : 0;\\n    const bFeatured = b.featured ? 1 : 0;\\n    if (aFeatured !== bFeatured) return bFeatured - aFeatured;\\n\\n    return a.sellingPricePaise - b.sellingPricePaise;\\n  });\\n  return copy;\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/shared/domainLogic.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Adding photo verification and integrity logic to domainLogic.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add photo verification logic to domainLogic.ts\"}"
