  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Admin Product Routes**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `server.ts` file, specifically lines 950-1200. My objective is to pinpoint the definition of Admin Product routes. From there, I\'ll integrate the server-side endpoints for `GET /api/product-image-report` and `GET /api/admin/product-image-report`, ensuring they accurately return what\'s expected.\n\n\n**Compiling Image Data**\n\nI\'ve successfully retrieved a comprehensive list of all ten existing products, meticulously joined with `product_image_audits`. This includes vital details like product ID, name, brand, variants, SKU, and existing images. I\'ve also tallied the counts for each of the five essential statuses. Plus, I just received verification that product integrity is unchanged, proving that the product count, along with crucial data like IDs and names, remains stable.\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for a protected `POST` endpoint, which is designed to query the Wikimedia Commons API using precise product details. The goal is to determine if any results align precisely with the product\'s brand and SKU.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Endpoint Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the logic for the `POST /api/admin/product-images/candidate/:productId` endpoint, which is protected by `requireAdmin`. I\'m focusing on ensuring it validates candidate image URLs or files comprehensively before proceeding. This involves checking HTTP status, content-type (JPEG, PNG, WebP), and byte size if a URL is provided. I\'ll be using `validateCandidateProductImage(...)` for this. The status will be set accordingly, without affecting published product images until approval. I want this endpoint to update the audit record precisely, reflecting the nature of any validation results, rather than fabricating outcomes.\n\n\n**Defining Approval Processes**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the admin image approval processes. I\'m building out the logic for the `POST /api/admin/product-images/approve/:productId` and `POST /api/admin/product-images/reject/:productId` endpoints, both protected by `requireAdmin`. For approval, I\'m ensuring it updates only `images_json` and `updated_at` on the product record, preserving all other data. Rejection will set the product audit status to \'Image Needed\' or similar, keeping the existing product images untouched.\n\n\n"
