    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Implement the **Original Product Photo Audit, Search, Verification & Admin Approval Workflow + Admin Image Report** for the **10 existing products** in the Pretty Charm SQLite database (`./data/pretty_charm.sqlite`).\n   - **Strict Invariants**:\n     - Do **not** create a new product list or add/remove/duplicate products.\n     - Keep all 10 existing product IDs, names, slugs, descriptions, SKUs, categories, variants, selling prices, and stock quantities **100% unchanged**.\n     - Do not substitute similar-looking third-party products or AI-generated images as genuine original product photographs.\n     - Do not assume third-party web results are licensed for commercial reuse.\n     - Show candidate previews and source URLs to the Admin for approval/rejection before updating any product\'s gallery (`images_json`), preserving existing images by default unless replacement is explicitly selected.\n     - Display the **Admin Image Report** with the exact 5 statuses:\n       1. `Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval`\n       2. `Image successfully added`\n       3. `Image Needed`\n       4. `Source or reuse permission unverified`\n       5. `Search failed`\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Previously**:\n     - Built the complete Pretty Charm storefront (`src/App.tsx`, 23 screens) and 15-section Admin Suite (`src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`), persistent SQLite database (`src/server/db.ts`), and full-stack Express server (`server.ts`).\n     - Implemented product sorting (`Price: Low to High`, `Price: High to Low`, `Newest Arrivals`, `Featured`) in `src/shared/domainLogic.ts` (`sortCatalogueProducts`) and wired it into `src/App.tsx` (`categories` and `shop` views).\n   - **Completed for Current Task**:\n     - **Step 1 (Inspected Existing 10 Products)**: Verified the exact 10 products in `./data/pretty_charm.sqlite`:\n       1. `prod-mini-hamper` (`Pretty Charm Mini Hamper`, `gift-hampers`, SKU `PC-HMP-MINI`, `draft`, \342\202\271299, stock `0`)\n       2. `prod-bestie-box` (`Pretty Charm Bestie Box`, `gift-hampers`, SKU `PC-HMP-BESTIE`, `draft`, \342\202\271299, stock `0`)\n       3. `prod-premium-box` (`Pretty Charm Premium Box`, `gift-hampers`, SKU `PC-HMP-PREM`, `draft`, \342\202\271449, stock `0`)\n       4. `prod-celebration-box` (`Pretty Charm Celebration Box`, `gift-hampers`, SKU `PC-HMP-CELEB`, `draft`, \342\202\271449, stock `0`)\n       5. `prod-pearl-claw` (`Rose Gold Pearl Hair Claw`, `hair-accessories`, SKU `PC-HAIR-CLAW-01`, `active`, \342\202\271249, stock `18`, 2 variants)\n       6. `prod-silk-scrunchie-trio` (`Mulberry Silk Scrunchie Trio`, `hair-accessories`, SKU `PC-HAIR-SCR-03`, `active`, \342\202\271199, stock `24`, 2 variants)\n       7. `prod-satin-bow-barrette` (`Blush Satin Pearl Bow Barrette`, `hair-accessories`, SKU `PC-HAIR-BOW-02`, `active`, \342\202\271179, stock `4`)\n       8. `prod-pearl-drop-huggies` (`Rose Gold Pearl Drop Huggies`, `jewellery`, SKU `PC-JWL-EAR-01`, `active`, \342\202\271349, stock `14`, 2 variants)\n       9. `prod-charm-bracelet` (`Dainty Rose Gold Charm Bracelet`, `jewellery`, SKU `PC-JWL-BRC-02`, `active`, \342\202\271399, stock `11`)\n       10. `prod-quartz-necklace` (`Blush Quartz Layered Necklace`, `jewellery`, SKU `PC-JWL-NCK-03`, `active`, \342\202\271429, stock `3`)\n     - **Step 2 (Web Search Verification)**: Ran `search_web` for all 10 existing products using exact names, brand (`Pretty Charm`), variants, and SKUs. Confirmed that Pretty Charm\'s SKUs (`PC-HMP-*`, `PC-HAIR-*`, `PC-JWL-*`) are bespoke Gurugram studio items; third-party boutiques (`queenmee.com`, `houseofwhitemulberry.com`, `jewelrybyshinestar.com`, `etsy.com`, `soleandbloom.in`) sell similar generic items without verified commercial image reuse permissions.\n     - **Pure Domain Logic & Unit Tests**:\n       - Updated `/src/shared/domainLogic.ts` (Section 11) with `ProductImageAuditStatus`, `PRODUCT_IMAGE_AUDIT_STATUSES`, `validateCandidateProductImage`, `applyApprovedProductImageToGallery`, and `verifyCatalogueIntegrityUnchanged`.\n       - Updated `/src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts` with Test #13 covering all 5 statuses, AI-image rejection, unverified reuse permission flagging, gallery preservation/primary image promotion, and catalogue integrity verification.\n     - **Database Schema & Seeding (`/src/server/db.ts`)**:\n       - Added `product_image_audits` table and seeded initial audit records for all 10 existing products (`7` marked `Image Needed`, `3` marked `Source or reuse permission unverified` with the discovered third-party URLs and reasons) plus `catalogue_integrity_baseline` in `store_settings`.\n     - **Backend Endpoints (`/server.ts`)**:\n       - Added `buildProductImageAuditReport()`, `GET /api/product-image-report`, `GET /api/admin/product-image-report`, `POST /api/admin/product-images/search/:productId` (live Wikimedia Commons API search), `POST /api/admin/product-images/candidate/:productId` (candidate URL/file validation), `POST /api/admin/product-images/approve/:productId` (updates only `images_json`), and `POST /api/admin/product-images/reject/:productId`.\n   - **Remaining / Incomplete**:\n     - Update `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx` to render the **Admin Image Report & Original Photo Approval Workflow** UI inside the `2. Products & Drafts` tab (showing the 5 status summary cards, before/after Catalogue Integrity check badge, table of all 10 existing products with image preview, source URL, status, reason, \"Search Permitted Sources\" button, \"Stage Candidate Original Photo\" form, and \"Approve / Reject\" controls with \"Preserve existing images\" and \"Set as primary image\" checkboxes).\n     - Run unit tests (`npx --yes tsx --test src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts`), `compile_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and verify via `playwright-cli` and `GET /api/product-image-report`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - Because HMR is disabled (`DISABLE_HMR=true`), always call `restart_dev_server` after editing frontend or backend files before running `playwright-cli`.\n   - When `server.ts` restarts, `initializeDatabase()` will automatically create `product_image_audits` and seed the 10 audit rows and `catalogue_integrity_baseline` in `./data/pretty_charm.sqlite`.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx` already receives `data.imageAuditReport` from `GET /api/admin/overview` (added in `/server.ts` line 1176).\n   - Lines 820\342\200\2231036 of `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx` contain the `activeTab === \'products\'` view where the **Admin Image Report & Original Photo Approval** panel should be added right above or below the Catalogue Table.\n\n5. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Update `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`**:\n      - Add state and handlers for `handleSearchProductPhoto(productId)`, `handleStageCandidatePhoto(e)`, `handleApproveProductPhoto(productId, replaceExisting, setAsPrimary)`, and `handleRejectProductPhoto(productId)`.\n      - Render the **Step 4: Admin Image Report & Original Photo Approval** section inside `activeTab === \'products\'` (with `data-testid=\"admin-image-report\"`), displaying the 5 status counts, the Catalogue Integrity Verification badge (`10 / 10 Products Unchanged`), and each product\'s name, SKU, current image preview, candidate preview, source URL, status, reason, and action buttons.\n   2. **Run Unit Tests, Compile & Restart Server**:\n      - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts` (all 13 tests must pass).\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `restart_dev_server`.\n   3. **Verify Integrity & UI in Headless Chromium (`playwright-cli`)**:\n      - Query `http://localhost:3000/api/product-image-report` and verify in Chromium that all 10 existing products, IDs, names, prices, categories, variants, and stock remain 100% unchanged before and after the task.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Never add, remove, rename, or alter any of the 10 existing products, their prices, descriptions, SKUs, categories, variants, or stock quantities.\n   - Never auto-publish unapproved or unlicensed images.\n</summary>"
