  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Constraints**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The `generate_image` tool returned a \"resource exhausted\" error, which, combined with the user\'s instructions, points to a likely quota limitation. I\'m focusing on how this impacts the overall strategy and whether I need to revise the approach.\n\n\n**Implementing the Fallback**\n\nI\'m adapting my approach due to the quota issue. The key is now ensuring the internet image search fallback and Gemini image generation fallback are both operational. I am now focused on using the Wikimedia Commons API and the server-side Gemini image generation, for CC-licensed images of the products, which will be our new Priority 1.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Sourcing**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust image sourcing strategy. If Gemini hits quota limits or has credential issues, I\'ll fall back *immediately* to a permitted internet image search using the Wikimedia Commons API. I\'m testing `run_command` right now to find CC-licensed product photographs for our six active products, ensuring we always have a viable image. I\'ll report Gemini credential status as needed, and will never fake image generation.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_373381"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"npx --yes tsx -e \\\"\\nconst queries = [\\n  { id: \'prod-pearl-claw\', q: \'hair claw clip OR pearl hair clip filetype:bitmap\' },\\n  { id: \'prod-silk-scrunchie-trio\', q: \'scrunchie hair filetype:bitmap\' },\\n  { id: \'prod-satin-bow-barrette\', q: \'pink hair bow OR ribbon barrette filetype:bitmap\' },\\n  { id: \'prod-pearl-drop-huggies\', q: \'pearl drop earrings filetype:bitmap\' },\\n  { id: \'prod-charm-bracelet\', q: \'charm bracelet gold filetype:bitmap\' },\\n  { id: \'prod-quartz-necklace\', q: \'rose quartz necklace OR rose quartz pendant filetype:bitmap\' },\\n];\\n\\nfor (const item of queries) {\\n  const url = \'https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&generator=search&gsrsearch=\' + encodeURIComponent(item.q) + \'&gsrnamespace=6&gsrlimit=5&prop=imageinfo&iiprop=url|extmetadata|mime|size&iiurlwidth=800&format=json\';\\n  const res = await fetch(url, { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'PrettyCharmCatalog/1.0 (https://prettycharm.in)\' } });\\n  const data = await res.json();\\n  const pages = Object.values(data?.query?.pages || {}) as any[];\\n  console.log(\'=== \' + item.id + \' ===\');\\n  for (const p of pages) {\\n    const ii = p.imageinfo?.[0];\\n    if (!ii) continue;\\n    console.log({\\n      title: p.title,\\n      thumbUrl: ii.thumburl || ii.url,\\n      fullUrl: ii.url,\\n      sourceUrl: ii.descriptionurl,\\n      mime: ii.mime,\\n      width: ii.width,\\n      height: ii.height,\\n      license: ii.extmetadata?.LicenseShortName?.value\\n    });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\\"\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Searching Wikimedia Commons API for permitted product photographs\", \"toolSummary\":\"Search Wikimedia Commons API for product photos\"}"
