  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Relevant Imagery**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing a Wikimedia Commons image, specifically \"File:White Pearl hair catch.jpg,\" associated with the \"prod-pearl-claw\" concept. It appears to be a white pearl hair claw. I need to understand its key visual attributes.\n\n\n**Identifying Accessory Images**\n\nI\'ve moved on to identifying images for additional products. I have found relevant photographic examples of scrunchies, a blush satin bow, and rose gold pearl drop earrings. The key is finding visuals that accurately represent the product and its key features. I am prioritizing finding and reviewing the associated imagery.\n\n\n**Acquiring Image Assets**\n\nI\'ve secured additional image resources, focusing on real-world examples. I\'ve found a studio photograph of pearl drop earrings, a close-up of a dainty gold charm bracelet, and a photograph of a rose quartz pendant necklace. I\'m now exploring the possibility of locally caching or generating high-resolution versions of these images to ensure reliability, performance, and validation within the project\'s image storage.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Integration**\n\nI\'m now focused on automating image import, as specified in Step 4. I\'m verifying image files, resolutions, and sources, then managing storage and associating images with product IDs. I\'m prioritizing setting images as primary where necessary and preserving existing images. I\'m also preparing for admin approvals for any necessary replacements of broken or mismatched images. I\'m also ensuring persistence, and I\'m aware of the admin image management in Step 5.\n\n\n**Defining Product Verification**\n\nI\'m now outlining a robust system to manage product image status, including clear indicators for each item: \"Genuine Image Found,\" \"Added Successfully,\" \"Awaiting Admin Approval,\" \"AI-Generated Image,\" \"Image Needed,\" and \"Search Failed.\" I\'m prioritizing safe approval workflows, especially if the project supports a safe approval workflow, allowing admin approval of multiple verified images. I\'m also planning to test integration with the storefront to confirm display across all relevant pages and areas, and the preservation of the Pretty Charm design and colors. Finally, I\'m testing downloading several real CC-licensed Wikimedia Commons photographs onto our server.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_389398"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"npx --yes tsx -e \\\"\\nimport fs from \'node:fs\';\\nimport path from \'node:path\';\\n\\nconst items = [\\n  {\\n    productId: \'prod-pearl-claw\',\\n    fileTitle: \'File:White_Pearl_hair_catch.jpg\',\\n    filename: \'prod-pearl-claw.jpg\'\\n  },\\n  {\\n    productId: \'prod-silk-scrunchie-trio\',\\n    fileTitle: \'File:Scrunchie_(386494891).jpg\',\\n    filename: \'prod-silk-scrunchie-trio.jpg\'\\n  },\\n  {\\n    productId: \'prod-satin-bow-barrette\',\\n    fileTitle: \'File:Pink_bow_for_wrapping,_2026-02-08_(side_view).jpg\',\\n    filename: \'prod-satin-bow-barrette.jpg\'\\n  },\\n  {\\n    productId: \'prod-pearl-drop-huggies\',\\n    fileTitle: \'File:Ian_Rosenberg_Jeweller_-_Silver_and_pearl_drop_earrings.JPG\',\\n    filename: \'prod-pearl-drop-huggies.jpg\'\\n  },\\n  {\\n    productId: \'prod-charm-bracelet\',\\n    fileTitle: \'File:Juicy_Couture_charm_bracelet_close_up.jpg\',\\n    filename: \'prod-charm-bracelet.jpg\'\\n  },\\n  {\\n    productId: \'prod-quartz-necklace\',\\n    fileTitle: \'File:Rose_quartz_pendant_necklace.jpg\',\\n    filename: \'prod-quartz-necklace.jpg\'\\n  }\\n];\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const outDir = path.resolve(\'./public/uploads/products\');\\n  fs.mkdirSync(outDir, { recursive: true });\\n\\n  for (const item of items) {\\n    const apiUrl = \'https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&titles=\' + encodeURIComponent(item.fileTitle) + \'&prop=imageinfo&iiprop=url|extmetadata|mime|size&iiurlwidth=800&format=json\';\\n    const metaRes = await fetch(apiUrl, { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'PrettyCharmCatalog/1.0 (https://prettycharm.in)\' } });\\n    const metaJson = await metaRes.json();\\n    const page: any = Object.values(metaJson.query.pages)[0];\\n    const ii = page.imageinfo[0];\\n    const downloadUrl = ii.thumburl || ii.url;\\n\\n    const imgRes = await fetch(downloadUrl, { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'PrettyCharmCatalog/1.0 (https://prettycharm.in)\' } });\\n