  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Product Assets**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed that all six active products now boast valid JPEG product photographs. Each file, downloaded and validated, is stored in the designated directory. They all have the proper dimensions and file size, and they\'re ready to go!\n\n\n**Verifying Image Licenses**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the legal side. I\'m carefully reviewing the Creative Commons licenses for each of the four product images I\'ve identified, making sure our usage complies with the specified attribution and source requirements. I am ready to move onto the next step of the project.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_467322"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"npx --yes tsx -e \\\"\\nimport fs from \'node:fs\';\\nimport path from \'node:path\';\\n\\nconst items = [\\n  { productId: \'prod-pearl-claw\', fileTitle: \'File:White_Pearl_hair_catch.jpg\', filename: \'prod-pearl-claw-thumb.jpg\' },\\n  { productId: \'prod-silk-scrunchie-trio\', fileTitle: \'File:Scrunchie_(386494891).jpg\', filename: \'prod-silk-scrunchie-trio-thumb.jpg\' },\\n  { productId: \'prod-satin-bow-barrette\', fileTitle: \'File:Pink_bow_for_wrapping,_2026-02-08_(side_view).jpg\', filename: \'prod-satin-bow-barrette-thumb.jpg\' },\\n  { productId: \'prod-pearl-drop-huggies\', fileTitle: \'File:Ian_Rosenberg_Jeweller_-_Silver_and_pearl_drop_earrings.JPG\', filename: \'prod-pearl-drop-huggies-thumb.jpg\' },\\n  { productId: \'prod-charm-bracelet\', fileTitle: \'File:Juicy_Couture_charm_bracelet_close_up.jpg\', filename: \'prod-charm-bracelet-thumb.jpg\' },\\n  { productId: \'prod-quartz-necklace\', fileTitle: \'File:Rose_quartz_pendant_necklace.jpg\', filename: \'prod-quartz-necklace-thumb.jpg\' }\\n];\\n\\n(async () => {\\n  const thumbDir = path.resolve(\'./public/uploads/products/thumbs\');\\n  fs.mkdirSync(thumbDir, { recursive: true });\\n\\n  for (const item of items) {\\n    const apiUrl = \'https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&titles=\' + encodeURIComponent(item.fileTitle) + \'&prop=imageinfo&iiprop=url|size&iiurlwidth=400&format=json\';\\n    const metaRes = await fetch(apiUrl, { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'PrettyCharmCatalog/1.0 (https://prettycharm.in)\' } });\\n    const metaJson = await metaRes.json();\\n    const page: any = Object.values(metaJson.query.pages)[0];\\n    const ii = page.imageinfo[0];\\n    const downloadUrl = ii.thumburl || ii.url;\\n\\n    const imgRes = await fetch(downloadUrl, { headers: { \'User-Agent\': \'PrettyCharmCatalog/1.0 (https://prettycharm.in)\' } });\\n    const buf = Buffer.from(await imgRes.arrayBuffer());\\n    const dest = path.join(thumbDir, item.f