  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Photo Storage**\n\nI\'ve successfully saved all the full-size product photos and their corresponding 400px thumbnails to disk. I am now transitioning to a thorough review of the original user prompt, so I can start to accurately design the next part of this.\n\n\n**Analyzing Product Inventory**\n\nI\'m currently focused on evaluating the existing product inventory. I am examining each active, for-sale item, identifying the product ID, name, SKU, price, stock quantity, and available variants. I\'m noting that the data is structured, which will help with the next steps, designing new backend logic for image storage, user prompt design, and database updates.\n\n\n**Evaluating Product Data**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the product data. The existing product data is unchanged in terms of names, prices, stock, variants, and other identifiers. The gift hampers remain in a \"draft\" status with the \"Image Needed\" label. Next, I am looking to automated image search for 6 active products.\n\n\n**Identifying Image Attributes**\n\nI\'ve just finished compiling image attributes for several more products. I\'ve noted the full-size and thumbnail file paths, image dimensions, and associated Creative Commons licenses, and found the links for each image.\n\n\n**Defining Image Generation Logic**\n\nI\'m now detailing fallback logic for image generation using Google Gemini. I am using the `@google/genai` library with the \'gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image\' model. My priority is crafting prompts exclusively from database product information. I am also planning to mark AI-generated images in the `product_image_audits` metadata.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Management**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the AI image generation into the admin dashboard. I\'ve ensured every action and status are included. There\'s a \"Find Images for All Available Products\" button, a \"Approve All Verified Candidates\" batch button, and a \"Review AI-Generated Images\" filter toggle. Per-product actions are in place, so admins can easily search for, retry, and approve the images. I\'ve also implemented error handling if generation fails.\n\n\n**Designing Admin Features**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the specific admin features for product image management. I\'ve designed the necessary buttons for different admin actions: image searching, AI generation, previewing, viewing the source, approving, and replacing images. Each button has a unique `data-testid` attribute for easy selection. I\'m also planning status badges to show the current image status.\n\n\n**Validating New Image Paths**\n\nI\'m now integrating validated, Creative Commons product photographs, ensuring they replace the current primary images and are marked as successfully added with full metadata. I\'m testing the admin dashboard workflows: \"Find Images,\" \"Preview Image,\" \"Approve and Add,\" and \"Replace Image\". Plus, I\'m verifying the Storefront\'s `src/App.tsx` updates, so the new product images appear across all relevant pages.\n\n\n"
