    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Management**\n\nI\'m currently focused on expanding `product_image_audits` and `domainLogic.ts` to fully meet task specifications. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of Admin Image Management statuses within `domainLogic.ts`, including \'Genuine Image Found\', \'Needs Review\', \'Suspect Image\', \'Image Removed\', and \'Needs More Information\'.\n\n\n**Expanding Image Functionality**\n\nI\'ve successfully added several new image statuses, including \'Awaiting Admin Approval\' and \'AI-Generated Image\'. I\'ve also incorporated \'Image Needed\' and \'Search Failed\' to reflect different scenarios. Backwards-compatible aliases are in place, too. Now, I\'ve started building out functions: `isProductEligibleForImageImport` for determining import eligibility and `buildGeminiProductImagePrompt` for creating accurate prompts. Finally, I\'ve planned an update for the `validateCandidateProductImage`.\n\n\n**Validating Image Types**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to validate image types. I handle local uploads, HTTPS URLs, and raster Data URIs. I\'ve also incorporated scenarios for AI-generated images. If `allowAiFallback` is enabled, I\'ll recommend the \'AI-Generated Image\' status. If `allowAiFallback` is false (strict mode), I\'ll reject AI images and recommend the \'Image Needed\' status. This approach ensures AI images are never misrepresented.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Schema Changes**\n\nI\'m now focused on database changes. I\'m adding new columns to `product_image_audits`, including `thumbnail_url`, `is_ai_generated`, `image_format`, `image_resolution`, and `image_bytes`. In `src/server/db.ts`, I\'m also defining and exporting `PERMITTED_COMMONS_PRODUCT_PHOTOS` to manage verified Creative Commons images for active products, detailing attributes such as source URL and license. Lastly, I\'ll update `seedInitialDataIfNeeded()` to import these photos into `products.images_json`.\n\n\n**Verifying Image Display**\n\nI\'m now checking image rendering across the site. I am specifically checking to ensure new primary images are displayed correctly, keeping existing SVG artwork as secondary gallery images. I\'ve updated the database, including the `product_image_audits`, with data like audit status, URLs, formats, resolutions, and `is_ai_generated` flags. I am now double-checking the display of category images in addition to the primary images, as the prompt directs me to.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_514306"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Update Section 11 of domainLogic.ts with Step 1-5 image statuses, eligibility check, local upload validation, AI fallback metadata labeling, and Gemini prompt builder\", \"EndLine\":1008, \"Instruction\":\"Update Section 11 in src/shared/domainLogic.ts to support the full set of Admin Image Management statuses, eligible available product filtering, local /uploads/products/*.jpg validation, AI-generated metadata labeling, and Gemini prompt construction from database fields.\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"// ============================================================================\\n// 11. ORIGINAL PRODUCT PHOTO VERIFICATION, APPROVAL & INTEGRITY AUDIT\\n// ============================================================================\\n\\nexport type ProductImageAuditStatus =\\n  | \'Genuine Image Found\'\\n  | \'Added Successfully\'\\n  | \'Awaiting Admin Approval\'\\n  | \'AI-Generated Image\'\\n  | \'Image Needed\'\\n  | \'Search Failed\'\\n  | \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\'\\n  | \'Image successfully added\'\\n  | \'Source or reuse permission unverified\'\\n  | \'Search failed\';\\n\\nexport const PRODUCT_IMAGE_AUDIT_STATUSES: ReadonlyArray<ProductImageAuditStatus> = [\\n  \'Genuine Image Found\',\\n  \'Added Successfully\',\\n  \'Awaiting Admin Approval\',\\n  \'AI-Generated Image\',\\n  \'Image Needed\',\\n  \'Search Failed\',\\n];\\n\\nexport function isProductEligibleForImageImport(product: {\\n  status: string;\\n  stockQty: number;\\n  reservedQty?: number;\\n}): boolean {\\n  const available = product.stockQty - (product.reservedQty || 0);\\n  return product.status === \'active\' && available > 0;\\n}\\n\\nexport function buildGeminiProductImagePrompt(product: {\\n  name: string;\\n  categorySlug: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  sku: string;\\n  variants?: ReadonlyArray<{ name: string }>;\\n}): string {\\n  const variantText =\\n    product.variants && product.variants.length > 0\\n      ? ` Known variants/colours: ${product.variants.map((v) => v.name).join(\', \')}.`\\n      : \'\';\\n  return `High-resolution e-commerce studio product illustration for Pretty Charm (${product.categorySlug}): \\\"${product.name}\\\" (SKU: ${product.sku}). Exact product details: ${product.description}.${variantText} Preserve known colours, materials, shape, and included components on a soft blush-cream studio surface. Do not invent unknown contents, text overlays, brand logos, or watermarks.`;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CandidateImageValidationInput {\\n  urlOrDataUri: string;\\n  sourceUrl: string;\\n  mimeType?: string;\\n  byteLength?: number;\\n  isAiGenerated?: boolean;\\n  allowAiFallback?: boolean;\\n  hasReusePermission?: boolean;\\n  exactProductMatch?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateCandidateProductImage(\\n  input: CandidateImageValidationInput\\n): {\\n  valid: boolean;\\n  recommendedStatus: ProductImageAuditStatus;\\n  isAiGenerated: boolean;\\n  reason: string;\\n} {\\n  if (input.isAiGenerated && !input.allowAiFallback) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      isAiGenerated: true,\\n      reason:\\n        \'Rejected: AI-generated images cannot be treated as genuine original product photographs.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.exactProductMatch === false && !input.isAiGenerated) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      isAiGenerated: false,\\n      reason:\\n        \'Rejected: Candidate image does not match the exact product, packaging, colour, and variant.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.hasReusePermission === false) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Source or reuse permission unverified\',\\n      isAiGenerated: Boolean(input.isAiGenerated),\\n      reason:\\n        \'Candidate image found on third-party domain, but commercial reuse permission or official brand authorization is unverified.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const rawUrl = String(input.urlOrDataUri || \'\').trim();\\n  const rawSource = String(input.sourceUrl || \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawUrl || !rawSource) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      isAiGenerated: Boolean(input.isAiGenerated),\\n      reason: \'Both a valid image preview URL/file and an attribution source URL are required.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const isHttpsUrl = /^https:\\\\/\\\\/[^\\\\s]+$/i.test(rawUrl);\\n  const isLocalUploadUrl = /^\\\\/uploads\\\\/products\\\\/[a-zA-Z0-9._/-]+\\\\.(jpg|jpeg|png|webp)$/i.test(\\n    rawUrl\\n  );\\n  const isRasterDataUri = /^data:image\\\\/(jpeg|jpg|png|webp);base64,[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+$/i.test(rawUrl);\\n  if (!isHttpsUrl && !isLocalUploadUrl && !isRasterDataUri) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      isAiGenerated: Boolean(input.isAiGenerated),\\n      reason:\\n        \'Image must be a validated HTTPS photograph URL, stored local product photograph, or a genuine JPEG/PNG/WebP photograph file.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.mimeType) {\\n    const allowedMimes = [\'image/jpeg\', \'image/jpg\', \'image/png\', \'image/webp\'];\\n    if (!allowedMimes.includes(input.mimeType.toLowerCase())) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        isAiGenerated: Boolean(input.isAiGenerated),\\n        reason: `Unsupported image MIME type \\\"${input.mimeType}\\\". Only real JPEG, PNG, or WebP photographs are accepted.`,\\n      };\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  if (typeof input.byteLength === \'number\') {\\n    if (input.byteLength < 128) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        isAiGenerated: Boolean(input.isAiGenerated),\\n        reason: \'Downloaded image file is empty or corrupted (< 128 bytes).\',\\n      };\\n    }\\n    if (input.byteLength > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        isAiGenerated: Boolean(input.isAiGenerated),\\n        reason: \'Image file exceeds the 10 MB safety limit.\',\\n      };\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.isAiGenerated && input.allowAiFallback) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: true,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'AI-Generated Image\',\\n      isAiGenerated: true,\\n      reason:\\n        \'Illustrative AI-generated image created from actual product attributes (not a physical photograph) \342\200\224 awaiting Admin review & approval.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    valid: true,\\n    recommendedStatus: \'Awaiting Admin Approval\',\\n    isAiGenerated: false,\\n    reason:\\n      \'Genuine product photograph validated (format, resolution, and permitted source license) \342\200\224 awaiting Admin approval.\',\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function applyApprovedProductImageToGallery(\\n  existingImages: readonly string[],\\n  approvedImageUrl: string,\\n  options: { replaceExisting: boolean; setAsPrimary: boolean }\\n): string[] {\\n  const cleanApproved = String(approvedImageUrl || \'\').trim();\\n  if (!cleanApproved) {\\n    return [...existingImages];\\n  }\\n\\n  if (options.replaceExisting) {\\n    return [cleanApproved];\\n  }\\n\\n  const filteredExisting = existingImages.filter((img) => img !== cleanApproved);\\n  if (options.setAsPrimary || filteredExisting.length === 0) {\\n    return [cleanApproved, ...filteredExisting];\\n  }\\n\\n  return [...filteredExisting, cleanApproved];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CatalogueIntegritySnapshot {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  slug: string;\\n  categorySlug: string;\\n  sku: string;\\n  sellingPricePaise: number;\\n  stockQty: number;\\n  status: string;\\n  variantSkus: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport function verifyCatalogueIntegrityUnchanged(\\n  before: ReadonlyArray<CatalogueIntegritySnapshot>,\\n  after: ReadonlyArray<CatalogueIntegritySnapshot>\\n): { unchanged: boolean; discrepancies: string[] } {\\n  const discrepancies: string[] = [];\\n\\n  if (before.length !== after.length) {\\n    discrepancies.push(`Product count changed from ${before.length} to ${after.length}.`);\\n  }\\n\\n  const beforeMap = new Map(before.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\\n  const afterMap = new Map(after.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\\n\\n  for (const [id, b] of beforeMap.entries()) {\\n    const a = afterMap.get(id);\\n    if (!a) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Existing product \\\"${b.name}\\\" (${id}) was removed.`);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    if (b.name !== a.name)\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} name changed from \\\"${b.name}\\\" to \\\"${a.name}\\\".`);\\n    if (b.slug !== a.slug) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} slug changed.`);\\n    if (b.categorySlug !== a.categorySlug) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} category changed.`);\\n    if (b.sku !== a.sku)\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} SKU changed from \\\"${b.sku}\\\" to \\\"${a.sku}\\\".`);\\n    if (b.sellingPricePaise !== a.sellingPricePaise) {\\n      discrepancies.push(\\n        `Product ${id} price changed from ${b.sellingPricePaise} to ${a.sellingPricePaise}.`\\n      );\\n    }\\n    if (b.stockQty !== a.stockQty) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} stock changed from ${b.stockQty} to ${a.stockQty}.`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.status !== a.status) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} status changed from \\\"${b.status}\\\" to \\\"${a.status}\\\".`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.variantSkus.join(\'|\') !== a.variantSkus.join(\'|\')) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} variants changed.`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const id of afterMap.keys()) {\\n    if (!beforeMap.has(id)) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Unexpected new product ID \\\"${id}\\\" was added.`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    unchanged: discrepancies.length === 0,\\n    discrepancies,\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"StartLine\":810, \"TargetContent\":\"// ============================================================================\\n// 11. ORIGINAL PRODUCT PHOTO VERIFICATION, APPROVAL & INTEGRITY AUDIT\\n// ============================================================================\\n\\nexport type ProductImageAuditStatus =\\n  | \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\'\\n  | \'Image successfully added\'\\n  | \'Image Needed\'\\n  | \'Source or reuse permission unverified\'\\n  | \'Search failed\';\\n\\nexport const PRODUCT_IMAGE_AUDIT_STATUSES: ReadonlyArray<ProductImageAuditStatus> = [\\n  \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\',\\n  \'Image successfully added\',\\n  \'Image Needed\',\\n  \'Source or reuse permission unverified\',\\n  \'Search failed\',\\n];\\n\\nexport interface CandidateImageValidationInput {\\n  urlOrDataUri: string;\\n  sourceUrl: string;\\n  mimeType?: string;\\n  byteLength?: number;\\n  isAiGenerated?: boolean;\\n  hasReusePermission?: boolean;\\n  exactProductMatch?: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport function validateCandidateProductImage(\\n  input: CandidateImageValidationInput\\n): {\\n  valid: boolean;\\n  recommendedStatus: ProductImageAuditStatus;\\n  reason: string;\\n} {\\n  if (input.isAiGenerated) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Rejected: AI-generated images cannot be treated as genuine original product photographs.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.exactProductMatch === false) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Rejected: Candidate image does not match the exact product, packaging, colour, and variant.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.hasReusePermission === false) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Source or reuse permission unverified\',\\n      reason: \'Candidate image found on third-party domain, but commercial reuse permission or official brand authorization is unverified.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const rawUrl = String(input.urlOrDataUri || \'\').trim();\\n  const rawSource = String(input.sourceUrl || \'\').trim();\\n  if (!rawUrl || !rawSource) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Both a valid image preview URL/file and an attribution source URL are required.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const isHttpsUrl = /^https:\\\\/\\\\/[^\\\\s]+$/i.test(rawUrl);\\n  const isRasterDataUri = /^data:image\\\\/(jpeg|jpg|png|webp);base64,[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+$/i.test(rawUrl);\\n  if (!isHttpsUrl && !isRasterDataUri) {\\n    return {\\n      valid: false,\\n      recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n      reason: \'Image must be a validated HTTPS photograph URL or a genuine JPEG/PNG/WebP photograph file.\',\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (input.mimeType) {\\n    const allowedMimes = [\'image/jpeg\', \'image/jpg\', \'image/png\', \'image/webp\'];\\n    if (!allowedMimes.includes(input.mimeType.toLowerCase())) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        reason: `Unsupported image MIME type \\\"${input.mimeType}\\\". Only real JPEG, PNG, or WebP photographs are accepted.`,\\n      };\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  if (typeof input.byteLength === \'number\') {\\n    if (input.byteLength < 128) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        reason: \'Downloaded image file is empty or corrupted (< 128 bytes).\',\\n      };\\n    }\\n    if (input.byteLength > 10 * 1024 * 1024) {\\n      return {\\n        valid: false,\\n        recommendedStatus: \'Image Needed\',\\n        reason: \'Image file exceeds the 10 MB safety limit.\',\\n      };\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    valid: true,\\n    recommendedStatus: \'Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\',\\n    reason: \'Verified matching product photograph from permitted source \342\200\224 awaiting Admin approval before publishing.\',\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function applyApprovedProductImageToGallery(\\n  existingImages: readonly string[],\\n  approvedImageUrl: string,\\n  options: { replaceExisting: boolean; setAsPrimary: boolean }\\n): string[] {\\n  const cleanApproved = String(approvedImageUrl || \'\').trim();\\n  if (!cleanApproved) {\\n    return [...existingImages];\\n  }\\n\\n  if (options.replaceExisting) {\\n    return [cleanApproved];\\n  }\\n\\n  const filteredExisting = existingImages.filter((img) => img !== cleanApproved);\\n  if (options.setAsPrimary || filteredExisting.length === 0) {\\n    return [cleanApproved, ...filteredExisting];\\n  }\\n\\n  return [...filteredExisting, cleanApproved];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CatalogueIntegritySnapshot {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  slug: string;\\n  categorySlug: string;\\n  sku: string;\\n  sellingPricePaise: number;\\n  stockQty: number;\\n  status: string;\\n  variantSkus: string[];\\n}\\n\\nexport function verifyCatalogueIntegrityUnchanged(\\n  before: ReadonlyArray<CatalogueIntegritySnapshot>,\\n  after: ReadonlyArray<CatalogueIntegritySnapshot>\\n): { unchanged: boolean; discrepancies: string[] } {\\n  const discrepancies: string[] = [];\\n\\n  if (before.length !== after.length) {\\n    discrepancies.push(`Product count changed from ${before.length} to ${after.length}.`);\\n  }\\n\\n  const beforeMap = new Map(before.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\\n  const afterMap = new Map(after.map((p) => [p.id, p]));\\n\\n  for (const [id, b] of beforeMap.entries()) {\\n    const a = afterMap.get(id);\\n    if (!a) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Existing product \\\"${b.name}\\\" (${id}) was removed.`);\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    if (b.name !== a.name) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} name changed from \\\"${b.name}\\\" to \\\"${a.name}\\\".`);\\n    if (b.slug !== a.slug) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} slug changed.`);\\n    if (b.categorySlug !== a.categorySlug) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} category changed.`);\\n    if (b.sku !== a.sku) discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} SKU changed from \\\"${b.sku}\\\" to \\\"${a.sku}\\\".`);\\n    if (b.sellingPricePaise !== a.sellingPricePaise) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} price changed from ${b.sellingPricePaise} to ${a.sellingPricePaise}.`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.stockQty !== a.stockQty) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} stock changed from ${b.stockQty} to ${a.stockQty}.`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.status !== a.status) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} status changed from \\\"${b.status}\\\" to \\\"${a.status}\\\".`);\\n    }\\n    if (b.variantSkus.join(\'|\') !== a.variantSkus.join(\'|\')) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Product ${id} variants changed.`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  for (const id of afterMap.keys()) {\\n    if (!beforeMap.has(id)) {\\n      discrepancies.push(`Unexpected new product ID \\\"${id}\\\" was added.`);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    unchanged: discrepancies.length === 0,\\n    discrepancies,\\n  };\\n}\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/shared/domainLogic.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating Section 11 of src/shared/domainLogic.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update Section 11 of src/shared/domainLogic.ts\"}"
