    thinking: "**Examining Server Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into `server.ts` between lines 1200 and 1600. The aim is to understand and update `buildProductImageAuditReport()` and the image management routes, which includes serving the `/uploads` directory statically using `express.static` at `/uploads`.\n\n\n**Refining Endpoint Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `/api/admin/product-images/find-all-available` endpoint. I\'m prioritizing the logic for finding images for all available products based on their `isProductEligibleForImageImport` status. The priority order is clear: official sources, then permitted internet searches, and finally, Gemini for image generation. I\'m also ensuring the `/uploads` directory is accessible for development and production. The aim is to ensure the product images and thumbnails are served as expected. I\'m preparing the update to `buildProductImageAuditReport()`.\n\n\n**Validating Image Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing file validation logic to confirm image format, resolution, and size. Upon successful validation, verified images will be either imported or staged, and an updated audit report will be returned. I\'m also working on the `/api/admin/product-images/search/:productId` endpoint, handling scenarios where a product image is available but requires validation before being used, and implementing the Wikimedia Commons API search. The Gemini fallback is also now implemented.\n\n\n"
