  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Verification Needs**\n\nI\'m currently meticulously dissecting the verification requirements. Right now, I\'m laser-focused on outlining the verification process for \"Journeys.\" I plan to create a roadmap for implementation and the checks required to ensure all criteria are met. The end goal is to make sure every aspect of the project is verified, to the highest possible standards.\n\n\n**Verifying Homepage Elements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to verifying specific homepage elements within Journey 1. I\'m checking that the Hero section displays the correct headline, supporting text, and CTAs. I\'m verifying the image, and also testing the navigation to Gift Hampers and Hair Accessories. Next, I will test the search functionality as well as the header navigation.\n\n\n**Validating Mobile Menu Behavior**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the mobile menu\'s behavior, particularly on smaller viewports. I\'m confirming it opens and closes smoothly across the various mobile screen sizes I\'ve defined. The primary concern is ensuring there\'s absolutely no horizontal overflow during any interaction. My aim is to deliver a perfectly fluid user experience, regardless of the device. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s accessible and intuitive.\n\n\n**Examining Responsive Designs**\n\nI\'m now methodically scrutinizing the responsive design across various screens and viewports. I\'m focusing on testing the homepage\'s display at 360px, 375px, 390px, 430px, 768px (tablet), and 1440px (desktop), all the while verifying `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= document.documentElement.clientWidth` at each width. This should cover the core dimensions and make sure there is no horizontal scrolling.\n\nI\'m also moving onto examining all the links in the footer, to be sure they link to the correct pages. I\'m focused on verifying \'About Us\', \'Contact\', \'FAQ\', \'Shipping Policy\', \'Returns and Refunds\', \'Privacy Policy\', \'Terms and Conditions\', and links to Instagram and WhatsApp support. I\'m taking a close look at Admin-configurable fields within `generalSettings`, specifically under `store_settings`, and within `AdminDashboard.tsx`.\nI\'m also looking at the Announcement Bar configuration, and `whyShopBenefits`.\n\n\n**Refining Header Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the header\'s implementation. I\'m focusing on the Pretty Charm logo and the layout of the search field, ensuring its accessibility and responsiveness across all devices, especially the smaller viewports. I\'m verifying the account, wishlist, and cart icons, along with the Admin button. I\'m also reviewing the navigation structure, including the mobile menu drawer to confirm the correct state is displayed.\n\n\n**Crafting Homepage Composition**\n\nI\'m now focused on the homepage\'s visual narrative. I\'m prioritizing the hero section\'s visual elements, featuring `pearl-claw.jpg` as the primary showcase. I\'m ensuring the headline, supporting text, and CTAs match the provided specifics, including the warm cream background and blush pink accents. I am aiming for zero clutter. I\'m now crafting the \"Shop by Category\" section, generating editorial category cards for each of the five database categories.\n\n\n**Constructing Product Displays**\n\nI\'m now building out the product displays on the homepage, focusing on the Featured Products section. I\'m verifying that only active and in-stock items are showcased. Each product card will display the correct image, name, price, and variant information. I will also incorporate the wishlist control and ensure proper links for viewing each product, to the finest detail.\n\n\n**Implementing Product Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Add to Cart\" interactions. I\'m prioritizing accuracy: no fake discounts, star ratings, or invented prices. I\'m verifying unavailable products are never displayed as purchasable. Next, I\'m integrating a Gift Hampers collection, using real product data from the database. I\'m focusing on an honest and transparent display, and a refined \"Brand Story\" editorial section to communicate our brand. I\'ll verify the \"Why Shop With Us\" section using Admin settings.\n\n\n**Verifying Feature Integrity**\n\nI\'m now methodically verifying the integrity of key features. I\'m confirming that the \"Thoughtfully selected products\" description accurately reflects curated items with transparent specifications. I\'m verifying the secure ordering process and accurate shipping rates based on location. I\'m ensuring there are no unsubstantiated claims, such as unverified free shipping or payment certifications.\n\n\n**Validating Footer Features**\n\nI\'m now methodically validating all the footer features. I\'ve confirmed that the links for \'About Us\', \'Contact\', \'FAQ\', \'Shipping Policy\', \'Returns and Refunds\', \'Privacy Policy\', and \'Terms and Conditions\' all work correctly and lead to the expected screens. I\'ve also verified the Instagram and WhatsApp support links, ensuring they correctly navigate to the relevant destinations. I\'ve also implemented a disabled placeholder for the Newsletter section, while we await an email backend. I\'m looking to refactor to improve code re-use.\n\n\n"
