    user_requests: "Implement a sorting feature in the product listing (Category Page) to allow users to sort products by \'Price: Low to High\', \'Price: High to Low\', and \'Newest Arrivals\'."
    user_requests: "# Pretty Charm \342\200\224 Find Original Photos for Existing Products Only\n\nInspect my existing Pretty Charm e-commerce project and database first.\n\n## Main Task\nUse the product list that ALREADY EXISTS in my project. Find genuine, matching product photographs for those exact products and add the approved photos to their existing product records.\n\n**Do not create a new product list. Do not add new products. Do not rename, remove, duplicate, or change existing products, prices, descriptions, SKUs, variants, categories, or stock.**\n\n## Step 1: Read Existing Products\nRetrieve all current products from the existing database or product catalogue, including:\n- Product name\n- Brand, if available\n- Category\n- Variant, colour, size, or model\n- SKU, if available\n- Existing image URLs\n- Product status\n\nCreate an internal checklist of these existing products. Preserve their original IDs and all existing information.\n\n## Step 2: Find Matching Original Photos\nFor each existing product:\n1. Search using its exact name, brand, variant, and SKU when available.\n2. Prefer the original manufacturer\'s or brand\'s official website.\n3. Check authorized supplier or distributor catalogues where image reuse is permitted.\n4. Verify that the image actually matches the product, packaging, colour, and variant.\n5. Check image quality and usage permissions.\n\nDo not substitute a similar-looking product for the exact product. Do not treat AI-generated images as genuine original product photographs. Do not assume Google Images results are licensed for reuse.\n\n## Step 3: Update Existing Product Records\nWhen a suitable, authorized image is found:\n- Show its preview and source to the Admin.\n- Allow the Admin to approve or reject it.\n- After approval, update the image gallery of that same existing product.\n- Keep the original product ID, price, description, stock, and all other fields unchanged.\n- Preserve existing images unless the Admin explicitly chooses to replace them.\n- Set the approved main image as the primary image only after confirmation.\n\nIf no exact, authorized image is found, leave the current image unchanged and mark the product \"Image Needed\".\n\n## Step 4: Admin Image Report\nDisplay a report of the existing products with these statuses:\n- Original image found \342\200\224 awaiting approval\n- Image successfully added\n- Image Needed\n- Source or reuse permission unverified\n- Search failed\n\nInclude product name, image preview, source URL, and the reason for each status.\n\n## Step 5: Technical and Safety Rules\n- Use real, configured search APIs or permitted sources only.\n- Do not invent search results or fake integrations.\n- Do not bypass website protections or licensing restrictions.\n- Keep API credentials on the server.\n- Validate downloaded image files before storing them.\n- Do not publish unapproved images.\n- Do not modify the approved Pretty Charm UI, existing routes, or other functionality.\n\n## Final Verification\nCompare the product list before and after the task. Confirm that the number of products, product IDs, names, prices, categories, variants, and stock remain unchanged. Report how many existing products have approved original images and how many still need images.\n\nStart by inspecting the existing project and its current product list. Do not rebuild the website or create sample products."
    user_requests: "# PRETTY CHARM \342\200\224 ADD PRODUCT IMAGES FOR ALL EXISTING AVAILABLE PRODUCTS\n\nWork directly inside my existing Pretty Charm e-commerce project.\n\n## MAIN OBJECTIVE\n\nInspect my existing product database and catalogue. For EVERY product that is currently available for sale, find and add a suitable product image.\n\nDo not ask me to search for images manually one by one. Automate as much of the workflow as possible.\n\nUse these sources in the following priority order:\n\n1. Official manufacturer or brand website.\n2. Authorized supplier or distributor catalogue.\n3. Internet image search using a configured search API or permitted source.\n4. Google Gemini image generation for products whose genuine original photos cannot be found.\n\nIMPORTANT: A Gemini-generated image is NOT an original photograph of a real product. Use genuine product photos whenever available. If a generated image is used, label it internally as AI-generated and do not misrepresent it as an actual photograph.\n\n## STEP 1 \342\200\224 INSPECT ALL EXISTING PRODUCTS\n\nRead the actual product records from my existing database.\n\nIdentify all products that are:\n- Active and available for sale.\n- In stock.\n- Missing a product image.\n- Using a broken, irrelevant, duplicate, or low-quality image.\n\nProcess every eligible existing product. Do not add duplicate products or create a new catalogue.\n\nDo not modify existing product names, prices, stock, variants, SKUs, descriptions, categories, or product IDs.\n\n## STEP 2 \342\200\224 SEARCH FOR GENUINE PRODUCT PHOTOS\n\nFor each eligible product:\n- Search using its exact product name, brand, model, colour, and variant.\n- Prefer official brand and manufacturer photos.\n- Verify that the image matches the actual product and packaging.\n- Prefer high-resolution, clean product photography suitable for an e-commerce website.\n- Use only sources and images whose reuse or import is permitted.\n- Keep the source URL and image attribution/licence details when required.\n\nDo not simply download the first image returned by Google. Do not use unrelated images, watermarked photos, fake packaging, or photos of a different variant.\n\n## STEP 3 \342\200\224 GOOGLE GEMINI IMAGE GENERATION FALLBACK\n\nIf a genuine product photograph cannot be found, use Google Gemini\'s supported image-generation capability, if available and properly configured, to create a high-quality illustrative product image.\n\nRequirements:\n- Use the actual product information already stored in the database.\n- Preserve known colours, materials, shape, and included components.\n- Never invent unknown product contents or claim that the generated result exactly represents the physical item.\n- Save the image as AI-generated in its image metadata.\n- Require Admin approval before publishing it as the product\'s image.\n- If Gemini image generation is unavailable or requires missing credentials, continue with the internet-search and manual-upload fallback. Do not pretend an image was generated.\n\n## STEP 4 \342\200\224 AUTOMATIC IMAGE IMPORT\n\nOnce a suitable image is found:\n1. Validate the image file, format, resolution, and source.\n2. Store it using the existing project\'s configured image storage.\n3. Associate it with the correct existing product ID.\n4. Set it as the primary product image if the product has no suitable existing image.\n5. Preserve any useful existing images in the product gallery.\n6. Generate a thumbnail or optimized version if the existing application supports it.\n7. Verify that the image persists after refreshing the page.\n\nDo not replace a correct existing image unnecessarily. If an existing image is broken or clearly mismatched, prepare the replacement for Admin approval.\n\n## STEP 5 \342\200\224 ADMIN IMAGE MANAGEMENT\n\nAdd or update the existing Admin Dashboard with:\n- Find Images for All Available Products\n- Search Images for One Product\n- Preview Image\n- View Source\n- Approve and Add\n- Replace Image\n- Retry Search\n- Review AI-Generated Images\n\nShow a clear status for each product:\n- Genuine Image Found\n- Added Successfully\n- Awaiting Admin Approval\n- AI-Generated Image\n- Image Needed\n- Search Failed\n\nIf the project supports a safe approval workflow, allow the Admin to approve multiple verified images together. Never publish uncertain or unapproved images automatically.\n\n## STEP 6 \342\200\224 STOREFRONT VERIFICATION\n\nAfter approved images are added, verify that they appear correctly in:\n- Home page product sections\n- Category pages\n- Product listing cards\n- Product detail pages\n- Search results\n- Cart and checkout, where product thumbnails are displayed\n\nPreserve the existing Pretty Charm design, colours"
    user_requests: "# PRETTY CHARM \342\200\224 PREMIUM HOMEPAGE REDESIGN\n\nAct as a senior e-commerce UI/UX designer and frontend developer.\n\nRedesign ONLY the homepage of my existing Pretty Charm e-commerce website.\n\nBrand: Pretty Charm  \nBusiness: Gift Hampers, Hair Accessories, Jewellery  \nFuture categories: Cosmetics & Beauty, Festive Collection  \nBrand aesthetic: Premium feminine, elegant, soft blush pink, warm cream, subtle rose gold.\n\n## 1. Inspect Before Editing\n- Inspect the existing project, homepage components, product database, routes, and available image assets.\n- Keep the existing framework, architecture, logo, brand identity, and working functionality.\n- Change the homepage design substantially, but do not rebuild the entire website.\n- Use real product data from the existing database. Do not invent products, prices, discounts, reviews, or stock.\n\n## 2. New Homepage Layout\n\n### A. Announcement Bar\nA slim, elegant top bar for an Admin-configurable announcement, such as a shipping offer. Do not display unverified offers or delivery promises.\n\n### B. Header\n- Pretty Charm logo.\n- Search products field.\n- Account, wishlist, and cart icons.\n- Clean navigation for Home, Gift Hampers, Hair Accessories, Jewellery, and Coming Soon categories.\n- Mobile-friendly menu and accessible controls.\n\n### C. Premium Hero Section\nCreate a beautiful, editorial-style hero featuring a real available Pretty Charm product or hamper image.\n\nHeadline:\n\"Little Things. Beautiful Moments.\"\n\nSupporting text:\n\"Thoughtfully chosen gifts and pretty essentials for moments worth celebrating.\"\n\nPrimary CTA: \"Shop Gift Hampers\"  \nSecondary CTA: \"Explore Accessories\"\n\nUse elegant typography, generous spacing, soft cream backgrounds, blush pink accents, and subtle rose-gold details. Avoid excessive gradients, clutter, oversized text, and generic stock-photo aesthetics.\n\n### D. Shop by Category\nCreate visually appealing category cards for:\n- Gift Hampers\n- Hair Accessories\n- Jewellery\n- Cosmetics & Beauty \342\200\224 Coming Soon\n- Festive Collection \342\200\224 Coming Soon\n\nUse suitable, relevant images. Coming Soon categories must not be purchasable.\n\n### E. Featured Products\nDisplay actual active, in-stock products from the existing database.\n\nEach product card should show:\n- Product image\n- Actual product name\n- Current selling price\n- Variant information when relevant\n- Wishlist control\n- View Product or Add to Cart action, according to the existing functionality\n\nDo not show fake discounts, fake ratings, invented prices, or unavailable products as purchasable.\n\n### F. Gift Hampers Collection\nAdd a dedicated section for available gift hampers with attractive image cards and a \"View All Hampers\" link.\n\nUse the real saved product information. Do not invent hamper contents.\n\n### G. Brand Story\nCreate a compact, elegant section communicating the idea of thoughtful gifting and beautiful everyday accessories.\n\nDo not invent company history, founder achievements, or manufacturing claims.\n\n### H. Why Shop With Us\nShow only verified benefits. Keep these configurable from Admin, such as:\n- Thoughtfully selected products\n- Secure ordering process\n- Shipping information\n- Customer support\n\nDo not claim free shipping, guaranteed delivery, or secure payment certification unless actually supported.\n\n### I. Instagram Section\nAdd a \"Follow Pretty Charm\" section with a link to the Admin-configured Instagram profile.\n\nDo not create a fake live Instagram feed or invent followers and customer posts.\n\n### J. Newsletter or Offers\nInclude an optional email signup only if a functioning, privacy-compliant backend exists. Otherwise, omit it or implement it as a clearly labelled disabled placeholder in development.\n\n### K. Footer\nInclude working links to:\n- About Us\n- Contact\n- FAQ\n- Shipping Policy\n- Returns and Refunds\n- Privacy Policy\n- Terms and Conditions\n- Instagram\n- WhatsApp support, if configured\n\nDo not create dead links.\n\n## 3. Product Images\nPrioritize genuine product photos already stored in the project or obtained from authorized sources.\n\nUse high-quality, correctly matched images. Preserve aspect ratios and use consistent image containers. Optimize image loading and provide graceful fallbacks for missing images.\n\nDo not claim AI-generated imagery is an original photograph of a physical product.\n\n## 4. Visual Design\n- Premium blush pink, cream, warm beige, and restrained rose gold.\n- Elegant typography with clear readability.\n- Spacious layout and consistent alignment.\n- High-quality product cards with subtle borders and restrained shadows.\n- Smooth, subtle interactions without excessive animation.\n- Consistent buttons, icons, spacing, and border radii.\n- No cluttered layout, excessive neon, or cheap-looking effects.\n\n## 5. Responsive Design\nTest the homepage at widths of 360px, 375px, 390px, 430px, tablet, and desktop.\n\nEnsure:\n- No horizontal overflow.\n- Search and navigation remain usable.\n- Product cards adapt correctly.\n- Images load without layout shifts.\n- Buttons are easy to tap.\n- Text remains readable.\n- Cart and account controls work.\n\n## 6. Functionality and Safety\n- Keep existing product routes, cart, checkout, login, and Admin functionality working.\n- Connect sections to real existing routes and database data.\n- Never hardcode product inventory or prices if the database already provides them.\n- Do not expose secrets or private customer data.\n- Do not modify checkout or payment behaviour as part of this homepage-only task.\n\n## 7. Final Verification\nImplement the redesign in the existing project, then run relevant lint, type-check, build, and available tests.\n\nReport which homepage files changed, which tests passed, and any missing images or incomplete features.\n\nStart by inspecting the existing homepage and implement the redesign directly. Do not stop after giving me a design proposal or mockup."
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
  }
}
