  user_input {
    user_response: "Update the existing Pretty Charm e-commerce website to implement a complete WhatsApp-assisted order and payment workflow. Modify the existing project rather than creating a separate demo.\n\nCUSTOMER FLOW\n1. Customers can browse hampers, hair accessories and jewellery.\n2. Hamper prices are \342\202\271299 and \342\202\271499.\n3. Customers can manage cart items, quantities and checkout.\n4. Collect customer name, phone number, complete delivery address and optional delivery instructions.\n5. Validate products, prices, stock and totals on the server.\n6. Create a unique order ID and persist the order in the database before opening WhatsApp.\n7. Set initial payment status to pending and order status to awaiting_payment.\n8. Provide a button labelled \"Order via WhatsApp\".\n9. Open a click-to-chat link to the configured business WhatsApp number with a URL-encoded personalized message containing order ID, product names, variants, quantities, item prices, total amount, customer name and delivery address.\n10. Clearly tell the customer to press Send in WhatsApp. Never claim the order was submitted merely because WhatsApp opened.\n11. If the customer returns without sending the message, the saved order must remain accessible on the website.\n\nADMIN WORKFLOW\n1. Protect the admin dashboard with server-side authentication and authorization.\n2. Show orders with order ID, products, customer details, total, created time, payment status and fulfilment status.\n3. Search and filter orders.\n4. Allow the admin to copy the customer\'s WhatsApp contact link and send a prefilled payment instruction message.\n5. Allow the admin to send a payment link or QR image manually through WhatsApp.\n6. Provide an admin-only action to mark payment received after the actual bank/UPI transaction has been checked.\n7. Record who changed payment status and when, with an audit log.\n8. After verified payment, allow the admin to confirm the order.\n9. Generate a prefilled order-confirmation WhatsApp message containing the order ID, items, amount and confirmation status.\n10. Provide a \"Send Confirmation via WhatsApp\" button. The button should open the correct WhatsApp conversation with the message ready to send.\n11. Do not claim that click-to-chat automatically sends a message. Automatic outbound messages require a correctly configured official WhatsApp Business Platform/API and applicable permissions/templates.\n\nPAYMENT SAFETY\n- Do not implement fake payment verification.\n- Never mark orders paid from screenshots, UTR text, WhatsApp messages or browser redirects alone.\n- Do not show payment success until an authorized admin verifies the actual transaction.\n- Keep payment status separate from order fulfilment status.\n- Do not assume a personal/minor UPI account is approved for merchant or commercial use. Keep live payment instructions configurable and show setup warnings until account eligibility is confirmed.\n- Do not store UPI PINs, passwords or sensitive payment credentials.\n\nMOBILE-FIRST QUALITY\n- Optimize for 360px, 375px, 390px and 430px phone widths.\n- No horizontal overflow.\n- Ensure checkout, cart and WhatsApp buttons are easy to use on a phone.\n- Preserve the existing Pretty Charm branding.\n- Implement database persistence, loading/error states, validation and useful success screens.\n- Test order creation, total calculations, WhatsApp URL encoding, admin permissions and order confirmation.\n- Update the README with setup and deployment instructions. Clearly report any missing credentials or tests that could not run.\n\nImplement the complete workflow in the existing codebase. Do not stop at a plan or static UI."
    items {
      text: "Update the existing Pretty Charm e-commerce website to implement a complete WhatsApp-assisted order and payment workflow. Modify the existing project rather than creating a separate demo.\n\nCUSTOMER FLOW\n1. Customers can browse hampers, hair accessories and jewellery.\n2. Hamper prices are \342\202\271299 and \342\202\271499.\n3. Customers can manage cart items, quantities and checkout.\n4. Collect customer name, phone number, complete delivery address and optional delivery instructions.\n5. Validate products, prices, stock and totals on the server.\n6. Create a unique order ID and persist the order in the database before opening WhatsApp.\n7. Set initial payment status to pending and order status to awaiting_payment.\n8. Provide a button labelled \"Order via WhatsApp\".\n9. Open a click-to-chat link to the configured business WhatsApp number with a URL-encoded personalized message containing order ID, product names, variants, quantities, item prices, total amount, customer name and delivery address.\n10. Clearly tell the customer to press Send in WhatsApp. Never claim the order was submitted merely because WhatsApp opened.\n11. If the customer returns without sending the message, the saved order must remain accessible on the website.\n\nADMIN WORKFLOW\n1. Protect the admin dashboard with server-side authentication and authorization.\n2. Show orders with order ID, products, customer details, total, created time, payment status and fulfilment status.\n3. Search and filter orders.\n4. Allow the admin to copy the customer\'s WhatsApp contact link and send a prefilled payment instruction message.\n5. Allow the admin to send a payment link or QR image manually through WhatsApp.\n6. Provide an admin-only action to mark payment received after the actual bank/UPI transaction has been checked.\n7. Record who changed payment status and when, with an audit log.\n8. After verified payment, allow the admin to confirm the order.\n9. Generate a prefilled order-confirmation WhatsApp message containing the order ID, items, amount and confirmation status.\n10. Provide a \"Send Confirmation via WhatsApp\" button. The button should open the correct WhatsApp conversation with the message ready to send.\n11. Do not claim that click-to-chat automatically sends a message. Automatic outbound messages require a correctly configured official WhatsApp Business Platform/API and applicable permissions/templates.\n\nPAYMENT SAFETY\n- Do not implement fake payment verification.\n- Never mark orders paid from screenshots, UTR text, WhatsApp messages or browser redirects alone.\n- Do not show payment success until an authorized admin verifies the actual transaction.\n- Keep payment status separate from order fulfilment status.\n- Do not assume a personal/minor UPI account is approved for merchant or commercial use. Keep live payment instructions configurable and show setup warnings until account eligibility is confirmed.\n- Do not store UPI PINs, passwords or sensitive payment credentials.\n\nMOBILE-FIRST QUALITY\n- Optimize for 360px, 375px, 390px and 430px phone widths.\n- No horizontal overflow.\n- Ensure checkout, cart and WhatsApp buttons are easy to use on a phone.\n- Preserve the existing Pretty Charm branding.\n- Implement database persistence, loading/error states, validation and useful success screens.\n- Test order creation, total calculations, WhatsApp URL encoding, admin permissions and order confirmation.\n- Update the README with setup and deployment instructions. Clearly report any missing credentials or tests that could not run.\n\nImplement the complete workflow in the existing codebase. Do not stop at a plan or static UI."
    }
  }
}
