  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 4
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Core Request**: Update the existing **Pretty Charm** e-commerce website to implement a complete **WhatsApp-assisted order and payment workflow** (modifying the existing codebase rather than creating a separate demo).\n   - **Customer Flow Requirements**:\n     1. Customers can browse hampers, hair accessories, and jewellery.\n     2. Hamper prices are **\342\202\271299** (`29900` paise) and **\342\202\271499** (`49900` paise) \342\200\224 update `prod-mini-hamper` (`\342\202\271299`), `prod-bestie-box` (`\342\202\271299`), `prod-premium-box` (`\342\202\271499`), and `prod-celebration-box` (`\342\202\271499`) so they are active and purchasable (`status = \'active\'`, `stock_qty = 12`, `confirmed_by_admin = 1`).\n     3. Customers can manage cart items, quantities, and checkout.\n     4. Collect customer name, phone number, complete delivery address, and optional delivery instructions.\n     5. Validate products, prices, stock, and totals on the server (`/api/checkout/validate` and `/api/checkout`).\n     6. Create a unique order ID (`orderNumber`, e.g., `PC-2026-1001`) and persist the order in SQLite **before** opening WhatsApp.\n     7. Set initial payment status to `pending` and order status to `awaiting_payment`.\n     8. Provide a button labelled `\"Order via WhatsApp\"` (both as the checkout submit action that saves the order first and on the post-order confirmation screen so the customer can open/re-open the WhatsApp chat).\n     9. Open a click-to-chat link (`https://wa.me/<storePhone>?text=...`) to the configured business WhatsApp number with a URL-encoded personalized message containing: Order ID, product names, variants, quantities, item prices, subtotal/shipping/total amount, customer name, phone, and complete delivery address (plus optional delivery instructions).\n     10. Clearly tell the customer to press **Send** in WhatsApp. Never claim the order was submitted to WhatsApp merely because WhatsApp opened.\n     11. If the customer returns without sending the message, the saved order must remain accessible on the website (persisted in `localStorage` as recent saved orders + accessible via the post-order screen & `GET /api/orders/:orderNumber` / `POST /api/orders/track`).\n   - **Admin Workflow Requirements**:\n     1. Protect the admin dashboard with server-side authentication and authorization (`requireAdmin` in `server.ts`).\n     2. Show orders with Order ID, products (with variants/quantities/prices), customer details (name, phone, full address, delivery instructions), total, created time, payment status (`pending`, `paid`, etc.), and fulfilment status (`awaiting_payment`, `confirmed`, `processing`, `packed`, `shipped`, `delivered`, `cancelled`).\n     3. Search and filter orders (by Order ID, customer name, phone, payment status, and fulfilment status).\n     4. Allow the admin to copy the customer\'s WhatsApp contact link (`https://wa.me/91<customerMobile>`) and send a prefilled payment instruction message via WhatsApp.\n     5. Allow the admin to send a payment link or QR image reference manually through WhatsApp (configurable payment link / UPI ID / QR image URL in Admin Settings & Integrations, with an explicit merchant account eligibility warning banner).\n     6. Provide an admin-only action to mark payment received (`payment_status = \'paid\'`) after the actual bank/UPI transaction has been checked (`POST /api/admin/orders/:id/verify-payment`), keeping payment status separate from order fulfilment status.\n     7. Record who changed payment status and when (`verified_by_admin_id`, `verified_by_admin_email`, `verified_at`), with an audit log entry (`writeAuditLog`).\n     8. After verified payment, allow the admin to confirm the order (`POST /api/admin/orders/:id/confirm` or `POST /api/admin/orders/:id/status` setting `order_status = \'confirmed\'`, gated on `payment_status.toLowerCase() === \'paid\'`).\n     9. Generate a prefilled order-confirmation WhatsApp message containing the Order ID, items, total amount, and confirmation status.\n     10. Provide a `\"Send Confirmation via WhatsApp\"` button that opens the customer\'s WhatsApp conversation (`https://wa.me/91<customerMobile>?text=...`) with the message ready to send.\n     11. Explicitly state in the UI that Click-to-Chat does not automatically send messages (automatic outbound messages require a configured official WhatsApp Business Platform/API and approved templates).\n   - **Payment Safety & Mobile Quality**:\n     - Never mark orders paid from screenshots, UTR text, WhatsApp messages, or browser redirects alone.\n     - Keep payment status separate from order fulfilment status.\n     - Show setup warnings that a personal/minor UPI account should not be assumed approved for merchant/commercial use until account eligibility is confirmed.\n     - Optimize for `360px`, `375px`, `390px`, and `430px` phone widths with zero horizontal overflow.\n     - Update `README.md` with setup and deployment instructions, and report any missing credentials or tests.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed Previously**:\n     - Redesigned the homepage (`/src/components/PremiumHomepage.tsx` and `/src/App.tsx`), verified at `360px`, `375px`, `390px`, `430px`, `768px`, and `1440px`, with all 14 unit tests in `/src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts` passing.\n   - **Completed in This Turn (Inspection & Planning)**:\n     - Read all required skills (`/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`, `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`, `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`, and `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/1_ecommerce_retail.md`).\n     - Inspected `/server.ts` (all 3,307 lines), `/src/server/db.ts` (all 1,223 lines), `/src/shared/domainLogic.ts` (all 1,200 lines), `/src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts` (all 564 lines), `/src/App.tsx`, and `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - **Hamper Pricing & Availability**: In `/src/server/db.ts`, `prod-mini-hamper` and `prod-bestie-box` are `29900` (`\342\202\271299`), while `prod-premium-box` and `prod-celebration-box` were seeded at `44900` (`\342\202\271449`) in `draft` status. In `initializeDatabase()` in `/src/server/db.ts`, we should run a safe idempotent SQL update so `prod-mini-hamper` (`29900`) and `prod-bestie-box` (`29900`) and `prod-premium-box` (`49900`) and `prod-celebration-box` (`49900`) are active (`status = \'active\'`, `confirmed_by_admin = 1`, `stock_qty = CASE WHEN stock_qty <= 0 THEN 12 ELSE stock_qty END`, `purchase_cost_paise = CASE WHEN selling_price_paise = 29900 THEN 12500 ELSE 21000 END`), and refresh `catalogue_integrity_baseline` in `store_settings` so catalogue integrity checks remain `unchanged: true`.\n   - **Existing Unit Tests Compatibility**:\n     - In `src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts`, Test #8 checks `getInitialPaymentStatusForMode(\'demo\') === \'Demo Mode - Not Paid\'` and `getInitialPaymentStatusForMode(\'manual\') === \'Awaiting Verification\'`.\n     - If we add `\'whatsapp\'` to `PaymentMode` (`\'whatsapp\' | \'demo\' | \'manual\' | \'razorpay\'`), `getInitialPaymentStatusForMode(\'whatsapp\')` can return `\'pending\'`, and `getInitialOrderStatusForMode(\'whatsapp\')` can return `\'awaiting_payment\'`, while preserving `\'demo\'` and `\'manual\'` return values so Test #8 continues to pass!\n     - In `server.ts`, `POST /api/checkout` should set `order_status = \'awaiting_payment\'` and `payment_status = \'pending\'` (and default store `paymentMode` to `\'whatsapp\'`), and return the prebuilt `whatsappOrderUrl` and `whatsappOrderMessage` alongside the saved order record.\n     - In `calculateFinancialReport` and `canReleaseReservationOnCancel` (`src/shared/domainLogic.ts`), support both case conventions (`\'Paid\'` / `\'paid\'`, `\'Pending\'` / `\'pending\'`, `\'awaiting_payment\'` / `\'Pending Confirmation\'`, `\'Confirmed\'` / `\'confirmed\'`) so financial reports, cancellations, and existing tests work seamlessly.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - Dev server is running on port 3000 (`http://localhost:3000`).\n   - Database is SQLite at `./data/pretty_charm.sqlite`.\n\n5. **Next Steps (in exact execution order)**\n   1. **Extend `/src/shared/domainLogic.ts`**:\n      - Add WhatsApp-assisted order & payment workflow helpers:\n        - `buildCustomerOrderWhatsAppMessage(order)` & `buildCustomerOrderWhatsAppUrl(storePhone, order)` (includes Order ID, product names, variants, quantities, item prices, subtotal, shipping, total amount, customer name, mobile, complete delivery address, and optional delivery instructions).\n        - `buildAdminPaymentInstructionWhatsAppUrl(customerPhone, order, paymentConfig)` (prefilled payment instruction message with optional payment link / UPI ID / QR URL).\n        - `buildAdminOrderConfirmationWhatsAppUrl(customerPhone, order)` (prefilled order-confirmation WhatsApp message containing Order ID, items, total amount, and confirmation status).\n        - `canAdminConfirmOrder(order, adminRole)` (enforces server-side admin role authorization and requires `paymentStatus` to be `\'paid\'` / `\'Paid\'` before confirming an order).\n        - Support `\'whatsapp\'` payment mode (`payment_status = \'pending\'`, `order_status = \'awaiting_payment\'`) in `getInitialPaymentStatusForMode`, `verifyManualPaymentByAdmin`, `canReleaseReservationOnCancel`, and `calculateFinancialReport`.\n   2. **Add Unit Tests in `/src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts`**:\n      - Add Test #15 covering: order total calculation with \342\202\271299 and \342\202\271499 hampers, initial `pending` / `awaiting_payment` states, customer `\"Order via WhatsApp\"` URL encoding and message fields, admin payment instruction & order confirmation WhatsApp URL generation, and admin permission/payment verification checks before order confirmation.\n   3. **Update `/src/server/db.ts` and `/server.ts`**:\n      - In `/src/server/db.ts`: Migrate the 4 hampers to `\342\202\271299` (`prod-mini-hamper`, `prod-bestie-box`) and `\342\202\271499` (`prod-premium-box`, `prod-celebration-box`) with `status = \'active\'`, `stock_qty = 12`, `confirmed_by_admin = 1`, set default `paymentMode = \'whatsapp\'` in `store_settings`, and update `catalogue_integrity_baseline`.\n      - In `/server.ts`:\n        - Update `POST /api/checkout` to persist orders with `payment_status = \'pending\'` and `order_status = \'awaiting_payment\'`, returning `whatsappUrl` and `whatsappMessage` in the response.\n        - Add `GET /api/orders/saved/:orderNumber` (or phone-verified lookup) so returning customers can always access their saved order even if they closed WhatsApp without pressing Send.\n        - Update `POST /api/admin/orders/:id/verify-payment` so authorized admins can mark payment received (`payment_status = \'paid\'`), recording `verified_by_admin_id`, `verified_by_admin_email`, `verified_at`, and bank/UPI reference in `payment_records` and `audit_logs` **without** automatically conflating payment status with order fulfilment status.\n        - Add `POST /api/admin/orders/:id/confirm` (and enforce in `/status`) so confirming an order requires verified payment (`payment_status === \'paid\'`), records an audit log, and returns the prefilled confirmation WhatsApp URL.\n   4. **Update Customer Storefront Checkout & Saved Order Flow in `/src/App.tsx`**:\n      - Ensure Checkout collects customer name, 10-digit phone number, complete delivery address, and optional delivery instructions.\n      - Provide the primary checkout button `\"Order via WhatsApp\"` (which first validates and saves the order in SQLite, persists the saved order in `localStorage` so it stays accessible if the customer returns without sending, transitions to the Order Saved & WhatsApp Handoff screen, and provides the direct `\"Order via WhatsApp\"` link + copyable message).\n      - Display a clear instruction banner telling the customer to **press Send in WhatsApp**, never claiming the message was sent automatically, and showing a \"Saved Orders on This Device\" bar in Cart/Checkout/Track Order so returning customers can resume any unsent order.\n   5. **Update Admin Order & Payment Workflow in `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`**:\n      - In Tab `6. Orders`:\n        - Add search bar (Order ID, customer name, phone) and status filters (`All`, `awaiting_payment`, `pending` payment, `paid`, `confirmed`, `shipped`).\n        - Show full order details: Order ID, created timestamp, itemized products/variants/quantities/prices, customer name, phone, full address, delivery instructions, separate **Payment Status** (`pending` / `paid` + who verified & when) and **Fulfilment Status** (`awaiting_payment` / `confirmed` / `processing` / `packed` / `shipped` / `delivered`).\n        - Provide Admin actions on each order:\n          1. **Copy Customer WhatsApp Link** (`https://wa.me/91...`).\n          2. **Send Payment Instructions / Link / QR via WhatsApp** (opens prefilled `wa.me` chat with configurable payment link/QR/UPI instructions).\n          3. **Mark Payment Received (Admin Verified)** (requires admin to confirm bank/UPI check + optional bank reference; records admin email & timestamp in audit log).\n          4. **Confirm Order** (enabled after payment is verified; updates fulfilment status to `confirmed` and logs to audit log).\n          5. **\"Send Confirmation via WhatsApp\"** button (opens customer\'s WhatsApp chat with prefilled order confirmation message containing Order ID, items, total amount, and confirmation status).\n        - Display clear notice that Click-to-Chat opens WhatsApp with a prefilled message for manual sending (automatic outbound messages require WhatsApp Business Platform API) and a merchant UPI account eligibility warning in Settings/Orders.\n   6. **Update `/README.md`** with complete setup, environment variable, payment safety, WhatsApp Click-to-Chat vs Business API, and deployment instructions.\n   7. **Verify**: Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts`, `lint_applet`, `compile_applet`, `restart_dev_server`, and verify end-to-end customer + admin journeys and mobile widths (`360px`, `375px`, `390px`, `430px`) with `playwright-cli`.\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Never fabricate payment verification or mark orders paid from UTR text/screenshots/redirects alone.\n   - Keep payment status separate from order fulfilment status.\n   - Never claim opening `wa.me` automatically sends a WhatsApp message.\n   - Ensure zero horizontal overflow across `360px`, `375px`, `390px`, and `430px`.\n</summary>"
