  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Server Updates**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the specific adjustments needed within `/server.ts`. My immediate priority involves integrating several functions from `./src/shared/domainLogic`. I\'m meticulously considering how `getInitialOrderStatusForMode`, `buildCustomerOrderWhatsAppMessage`, `buildCustomerOrderWhatsAppUrl`, and `buildCustomer` will be incorporated. These additions will be central to how the server processes orders.\n\n\n**Integrating Payment Methods**\n\nI\'m now expanding the focus to include admin features within `/server.ts`. I need to integrate functions for generating admin-specific WhatsApp messages and URLs related to payment instructions and order confirmations. This includes `buildAdminPaymentInstructionWhatsAppMessage`, `buildAdminPaymentInstructionWhatsAppUrl`, `canAdminConfirmOrder`, `buildAdminOrderConfirmationWhatsAppMessage`, and `buildAdminOrderConfirmationWhatsAppUrl`. The `/api/storefront` route will need adjustments to incorporate payment mode and manual payment details, and the `/api/checkout` route is being updated for payment status.\n\n\n**Expanding Order Details**\n\nI\'m presently focusing on enhancing order details across several API endpoints. I plan to include `whatsappOrderUrl` and `whatsappOrderMessage` in the JSON responses for new orders and duplicates. Also, in the `/api/orders/track` endpoint, I need to add `shippingAddress`, `whatsappOrderUrl`, and `whatsappOrderMessage`. Furthermore, I\'m updating `computeFullAdminOverview()` to include more orders and additional details like verification timestamps, admin IDs, WhatsApp contact URLs, and payment instruction links.\n\n\n**Refining Payment Verification**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the payment verification process within `/api/admin/orders/:id/verify-payment`. The central idea is to decouple payment status from order fulfillment. When the admin verifies a payment, I will update the `payment_records` with detailed payment information and mark the `orders` entry as \'paid.\' Crucially, I\'m NOT automatically changing the order status to \'confirmed\'; that will be a separate action, keeping payment and fulfilment statuses distinct, as required. Also, I\'ll need to remember to record the audit log for `PAYMENT_VERIFIED`.\n\n\n**Implementing Order Confirmation**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing the `/api/admin/orders/:id/confirm` endpoint, ensuring it leverages `canAdminConfirmOrder`. It will strictly enforce that payment is \'paid\' before confirming the order. Upon confirmation, I\'ll update the order status, append to the status history, create the audit log entry, and return a confirmation message with its URL. I am updating `/api/admin/orders/:id/status` endpoint to support order status as title or lower case and gates the confirm order only if the payment is `paid`.\n\n\n"
