    thinking: "**Analyzing Customer Flow**\n\nOkay, I\'m digging into `/src/App.tsx` now, and my focus is on fortifying the Customer Flow. My primary concern is making sure the saved orders persistence, using `localStorage` and `lastVisited`, is bulletproof and meets all requirements. I\'m taking the steps required to ensure this is perfectly integrated within the customer flow, so that it\'s robust.\n\n\n**Refining Order Persistence**\n\nI\'ve just added order persistence to local storage. When a customer places an order via WhatsApp, the server now validates everything and creates a unique order number *before* opening WhatsApp. Simultaneously, `lastCreatedOrder` is saved, and prepended to the `savedOrders` array in local storage, so that even a page refresh won\'t lose the order. I\'ve also updated the checkout button label.\n\n\n**Finalizing WhatsApp Handoff**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the post-checkout screen\'s functionality. The user will see the unique Order ID and status, along with a clear notice about the WhatsApp send step. I\'m ensuring the \"Order via WhatsApp\" button accurately directs the customer to their pre-filled message, and the saved order persists even if the message isn\'t sent immediately. The order remains accessible.\n\n\n"
