  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Admin Workflow**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating the complete WhatsApp order and payment workflow into `/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`. I\'ve added state variables to handle order search, filtering by status and payment type, and tracking the confirmation process for specific order IDs. The next step is to implement the `handleConfirmOrder` function, which will use a `POST` request to confirm the order.\n\n\n**Refining Verification Processes**\n\nI\'m now integrating the order confirmation flow and enhancing the manual payment verification. I\'m focusing on the `/api/admin/orders/${order.id}/confirm` endpoint, ensuring audit logs and dashboard refreshes. I am also working on `handleVerifyManualPayment` to include admin entry of bank/UPI references, tracking who verified the payment, and ensuring the audit logs are updated. Additionally, I am designing a prominent \"Payment Safety & WhatsApp Click-to-Chat Notice Banner\" for the Orders tab, clarifying payment validation and WhatsApp communication limitations.\n\n\n**Designing Order Card Details**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the admin order cards. I\'m focusing on the UI elements, including a clear distinction between payment and fulfillment statuses. I need to make sure there\'s a good search and filter bar for order ID, status, and payment type. Also, I\'m integrating a quick configuration bar for payment links, UPI, and QR codes. Importantly, there will be a warning for merchant accounts, and that personal accounts shouldn\'t be used.\n\n\n**Detailing Order Card Sections**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the display of detailed order information within the admin order cards. I\'m prioritizing clarity and logical grouping of data. I\'ve designed sections for total amount, customer and delivery details, itemized product lists. I\'m now detailing the \"Customer WhatsApp Contact & Payment Instructions\" with copyable WhatsApp links and buttons for sending payment instructions. The next part will cover the admin payment verification step.\n\n\n**Finalizing Order Verification**\n\nI\'m now detailing the admin\'s payment verification workflow for the order cards. I\'m adding input fields for the Bank/UPI reference if the order isn\'t yet paid, along with a \"Mark Payment Received (Bank/UPI Checked)\" button. Then, the \"Confirm Order\" button is enabled after payment, initiating `handleConfirmOrder` to set order status to \'confirmed\'. I\'m also including a \"Send Confirmation via WhatsApp\" button or link opening the customer\'s WhatsApp with a prefilled confirmation. The current focus also is the prefilled preview.\n\n\n"
