  code_action {
    action_spec {
      command {
        instruction: "Update README.md with WhatsApp-assisted order and payment workflow documentation, payment safety warnings, unit test instructions, and deployment guide"
        is_edit: true
        file {
          absolute_uri: "file:///README.md"
        }
        use_fast_apply: true
        replacement_chunks {
          target_content: "# Pretty Charm \342\200\224 E-Commerce Platform & Operations Suite\n\n**Pretty Charm** is a complete, full-stack Indian e-commerce platform and inventory/accounting administration suite built for shipping curated gift hampers, hair accessories, and anti-tarnish demifine jewellery from **Gurugram, Haryana (122001)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n- **Frontend**: React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + Three.js (`ThreeHamperViewer`) + `vite-plugin-pwa` installable Progressive Web App.\n- **Backend**: Express + TypeScript (`server.ts`) running on port `3000`.\n- **Database**: Built-in Node 22 SQLite (`node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync`) stored persistently at `./data/pretty_charm.sqlite` with WAL concurrency and `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` ACID transactions.\n- **Pure Domain Logic & Tests**: `src/shared/domainLogic.ts` and `src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts` (11 unit tests covering integer paise math, shipping rules, Weighted Average Cost, stock reservation, payment safeguards, and spreadsheet formula-injection sanitization).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Local Setup (Windows, macOS & Linux)\n\n### Prerequisites\n- **Node.js 22.6+** (includes native `node:sqlite`).\n\n### Installation & Running Locally\n```bash\n# 1. Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# 2. Copy environment configuration\ncp .env.example .env\n# (On Windows PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)\n\n# 3. Run unit tests\nnpm test\n```\n\n# 4. Start development server on http://localhost:3000\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Admin Bootstrap & Authentication\n\n1. Set `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN` in `.env` (or use the local development fallback token `pretty-charm-bootstrap-2025` when `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN` is unset).\n2. Open the application and click **Admin** in the top bar.\n3. On first run, enter your Owner Name, Email, Strong Password (minimum 8 characters), and the Bootstrap Token to create the initial Owner Administrator account.\n4. Once created, bootstrap is permanently locked and all subsequent admin logins require your email and password.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Shipping, Payment & Courier Configuration\n\n- **Shipping Rules (INR)**:\n  - Subtotal `< \342\202\271499`: **\342\202\27159**\n  - Subtotal `\342\202\271499 \342\200\223 \342\202\271998`: **\342\202\27139**\n  - Subtotal `\342\211\245 \342\202\271999`: **Free Shipping**\n- **Payment Modes**:\n  - `manual_upi`: Displays your configured UPI ID (`prettycharm@upi`). Customers submit their 12-digit UTR reference; orders remain `Pending Verification` until an Admin explicitly verifies the bank credit in the Admin Panel.\n  - `cod`: Cash on Delivery.\n- **Shiprocket Courier Webhook**:\n  - Point your Shiprocket webhook to `POST /api/webhooks/shiprocket` with header `x-api-key: <SHIPROCKET_WEBHOOK_TOKEN>`. Duplicate webhook payloads are idempotently ignored via SHA-256 payload hashing.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Database Backup & Restore\n\n- **Backup**: Copy `./data/pretty_charm.sqlite` to a secure backup location, or export all 10 business reports (`.xlsx` / `.csv`) from **Admin Suite \342\206\222 Reports & Exports**.\n- **Production Build**:\n  ```bash\n  npm run build\n  npm start\n  ```"
          replacement_content: "# Pretty Charm \342\200\224 E-Commerce Platform & WhatsApp-Assisted Order / Payment Suite\n\n**Pretty Charm** is a full-stack Indian e-commerce platform and inventory/accounting administration suite built for shipping curated gift hampers (**\342\202\271299** and **\342\202\271499**), satin hair accessories, and anti-tarnish demifine jewellery from **Gurugram, Haryana (PIN 122001)**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Overview\n\n- **Frontend**: React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + Three.js (`ThreeHamperViewer`) + `vite-plugin-pwa` installable Progressive Web App, optimized for `360px`, `375px`, `390px`, and `430px` mobile screens with zero horizontal overflow.\n- **Backend**: Express + TypeScript (`server.ts`) running on port `3000`.\n- **Database**: Built-in Node 22 SQLite (`node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync`) stored persistently at `./data/pretty_charm.sqlite` with WAL concurrency and `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` ACID transactions.\n- **Pure Domain Logic & Tests**: `src/shared/domainLogic.ts` and `src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts` (15 unit test suites covering integer paise math, \342\202\271299/\342\202\271499 hamper totals, shipping rules, Weighted Average Cost, stock reservation, WhatsApp URL encoding, admin payment verification safeguards, order confirmation checks, and spreadsheet formula-injection sanitization).\n\n---\n\n## 2. WhatsApp-Assisted Order & Payment Workflow\n\n### Customer Flow\n1. **Browse & Cart**: Customers browse Gift Hampers (**\342\202\271299** and **\342\202\271499**), Hair Accessories, and Jewellery, and manage quantities in their cart.\n2. **Checkout & Server Validation**: Customers enter their full name, 10-digit Indian mobile number, complete delivery address, and optional delivery instructions. The server validates products, prices, stock, and totals (`POST /api/checkout/validate` and `POST /api/checkout`).\n3. **Database Persistence Before WhatsApp**: Clicking **\"Order via WhatsApp\"** first creates a unique Order ID (e.g., `PC-2026-1001`) and saves the order in SQLite with initial `payment_status = \'pending\'` and `order_status = \'awaiting_payment\'` **before** opening WhatsApp.\n4. **Click-to-Chat Handoff**: Opens `https://wa.me/<STORE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER>?text=...` with a URL-encoded personalized message containing the Order ID, product names, variants, quantities, item prices, subtotal, shipping fee, total amount, customer name, phone number, and complete delivery address.\n5. **Honest User Guidance & Saved Order Recovery**: Customers are explicitly told to press **Send** inside WhatsApp (opening WhatsApp never marks a message as automatically sent). If a customer returns without sending the message, their saved order remains accessible on the website (`localStorage` + `POST /api/orders/track`).\n\n### Admin Workflow\n1. **Protected Admin Dashboard**: Protected by server-side session authentication and role authorization (`requireAdmin` middleware).\n2. **Order Management, Search & Filtering**: View all orders with Order ID, created timestamp, itemized products/variants/quantities/prices, customer details, separate **Payment Status** (`pending` / `paid`), and **Fulfilment Status** (`awaiting_payment` / `confirmed` / `processing` / `packed` / `shipped` / `delivered` / `cancelled`). Filter by status or search by Order ID, customer name, or phone.\n3. **Manual Payment Instructions via WhatsApp**: Copy the customer\'s WhatsApp contact link (`https://wa.me/91<mobile>`) or click **\"Send Payment Instructions / Link / QR via WhatsApp\"** to open a prefilled chat containing your configured payment link, merchant UPI ID, or QR image URL.\n4. **Admin-Only Payment Verification & Audit Log**: After checking the actual bank/UPI transaction statement, click **\"Mark Payment Received (Bank Checked)\"** (`POST /api/admin/orders/:id/verify-payment`). Records `verified_by_admin_id`, `verified_by_admin_email`, `verified_at`, and bank/UPI reference in `payment_records` and `audit_logs`, keeping payment status separate from order fulfilment status.\n5. **Order Confirmation & Prefilled WhatsApp Confirmation**: Once payment is verified (`payment_status = \'paid\'`), click **\"Confirm Order\"** (`POST /api/admin/orders/:id/confirm`), then click **\"Send Confirmation via WhatsApp\"** to open the customer\'s WhatsApp conversation with the prefilled order confirmation message ready to send.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Payment Safety & WhatsApp Integration Warnings\n\n- **No Fake Payment Verification**: Orders are **never** marked paid from screenshots, customer UTR text, WhatsApp messages, or browser redirects alone. Only an authenticated Admin can mark an order `paid` after verifying the credit in the actual bank/UPI account.\n- **Merchant Account Eligibility Warning**: Do **not** assume a personal or minor savings/UPI account is approved for commercial/merchant use. Confirm merchant account eligibility with your bank or payment gateway before accepting live customer payments.\n- **Click-to-Chat vs Official WhatsApp Business API**: Click-to-Chat (`wa.me`) links open WhatsApp with a prefilled message that requires the user or admin to press **Send** manually. Automatic outbound WhatsApp messages require a configured official WhatsApp Business Platform/Cloud API account and approved message templates.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Local Setup & Running Tests\n\n### Prerequisites\n- **Node.js 22.6+** (includes native `node:sqlite`).\n\n### Installation & Running Locally\n```bash\n# 1. Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# 2. Copy environment configuration\ncp .env.example .env\n\n# 3. Run the 15 domain logic & WhatsApp workflow unit tests\nnpx tsx --test src/shared/domainLogic.test.ts\n\n# 4. Start development server on http://localhost:3000\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Admin Bootstrap & Production Deployment\n\n1. Configure `ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN`, `STORE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER`, and `SESSION_SECRET` in `.env`.\n2. Open the application and click **Admin** in the top navigation bar to bootstrap or sign in to the Owner Admin account.\n3. **Production Build & Start**:\n   ```bash\n   npm run build\n   npm start\n   ```\n"
          start_line: 1
          end_line: 70
        }
      }
    }
    action_result {
    }
    use_fast_apply: true
    description: "Update README.md with complete WhatsApp-assisted order & payment workflow, payment safety, setup, and deployment instructions"
  }
